export const mifDocsPages = {
  "mif-arch": {
    "id": "mif-arch",
    "title": "7.1: MIF Integration Scripts Architecture & Internal Mechanics",
    "subtitle": "Deep-dive into ScriptCacheImpl, JSR223ScriptDriver, and Invocable.invokeFunction lifecycle.",
    "html": "<h1>7.1: MIF Integration Scripts Architecture & Internal Mechanics</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">Deep-dive into ScriptCacheImpl, JSR223ScriptDriver, and Invocable.invokeFunction lifecycle.</p>\n<section>\n<p>Historically, customizing the Maximo Integration Framework (MIF) required writing custom Java classes (<code>UserExit</code>, <code>ExternalExit</code>, <code>MosProcess</code>), compiling JAR files, and rebuilding/redeploying the Maximo Enterprise Application Archive (EAR).</p>\n<p>With <strong>Integration Automation Scripts</strong>, developers can implement real-time business logic directly in <strong>Jython (Python)</strong> or <strong>JavaScript (Nashorn)</strong> without application server downtime or recompilation.</p>\n<h3>Internal Java Execution Lifecycle</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Script Discovery & Compilation</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>When Maximo initializes or when a script with <code>INTERFACE = 1</code> is created or modified in the <code>AUTOSCRIPT</code> table, ScriptCacheImpl.java loads the script into memory.</li>\n<li>JSR223ScriptDriver.java compiles the script and stores its compiled <code>ScriptEngine</code> reference in the internal <code>invocableScriptCache</code> map.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Procedural Scripts vs Function Library Scripts</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Standard Scripts (<code>INTERFACE = 0</code>)</strong>: Executed top-to-bottom sequentially from Line 1 to the end when triggered.</li>\n<li><strong>Integration Callback Scripts (<code>INTERFACE = 1</code>)</strong>: Structured as function libraries containing specific lifecycle hooks (such as <code>beforeProcess</code>, <code>beforeMboData</code>, <code>skipMbo</code>). The Maximo Java engine invokes only the required hook on-demand using Java's <code>Invocable.invokeFunction(\"functionName\", args)</code> mechanism.</li>\n<p></ul>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\"><div class=\"ibm-code-header\"><span>Architecture Flowchart / Diagram</span></div><pre class=\"flowchart-pre\">flowchart TD\n    subgraph CoreEngine [Maximo Scripting Engine]\n        DB[(AUTOSCRIPT Table)] --&gt; ScriptCache[ScriptCacheImpl.java]\n        ScriptCache --&gt; Driver[JSR223ScriptDriver.java]\n        Driver --&gt; CacheMap[(invocableScriptCache)]\n    end</p>\n<p>subgraph MIF_Pipeline [MIF Invocations]\n        PC[Publish Channel / ES / IC] --&gt; Exits[ScriptExternalExit / ScriptUserExit]\n        MOS[Object Structure Engine] --&gt; MOSProcess[MosProcessImpl / MosDefinitionImpl]\n        EndPoint[EndPoint Handler] --&gt; Router[ScriptRouterHandler]\n    end</p>\n<p>Exits --&gt;|invokeFunction| Driver\n    MOSProcess --&gt;|invokeFunction| Driver\n    Router --&gt;|invokeFunction| Driver</pre></div></p>\n</section>",
    "title_hi": "7.1: MIF Integration Scripts Kya Hote Hain aur Kaise Run Hote Hain?",
    "subtitle_hi": "ScriptCacheImpl, JSR223ScriptDriver aur Invocable.invokeFunction ka internal backend working.",
    "html_hi": "<h1>7.1: MIF Integration Scripts Kya Hote Hain aur Kaise Run Hote Hain?</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">ScriptCacheImpl, JSR223ScriptDriver aur Invocable.invokeFunction ka internal backend working.</p>\n<section>\n<p>Maximo Integration Framework (MIF) me pehle customization ke liye custom Java classes (<code>UserExit</code>, <code>ExternalExit</code>, <code>MosProcess</code>) likh kar EAR file rebuild aur redeploy karni padti thi.</p>\n<p><strong>Integration Automation Scripts</strong> aane ke baad aap direct <strong>Jython/Python</strong> ya <strong>JavaScript (Nashorn)</strong> me bina server restart kiye real-time business logic likh sakte hain.</p>\n<h3>Backend Java Code Me Ye Kaise Execute Hoti Hai?</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Jab Maximo start hota hai ya koi script save hoti hai (<code>AUTOSCRIPT</code> table me <code>INTERFACE = 1</code> set hota hai), toh ScriptCacheImpl.java is script ko load karta hai.</li>\n<li>JSR223ScriptDriver.java is script ko pre-compile karke <code>invocableScriptCache</code> map me daal deta hai.</li>\n<li><strong>Normal Object/Attribute Scripts vs Integration Scripts:</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Normal Scripts</strong>: Upar se niche (top-to-bottom) sequentially run hoti hain.</li>\n<li><strong>Integration Scripts</strong>: Inme specific <strong>lifecycle functions</strong> (jaise <code>beforeProcess</code>, <code>beforeMboData</code>, <code>skipMbo</code>) define kiye jaate hain. Maximo Java engine runtime par Java ke <code>Invocable.invokeFunction(\"functionName\", args)</code> ke zariye sirf wahi required function call karta hai.</li>\n<p></ul>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\"><div class=\"ibm-code-header\"><span>Architecture Flowchart / Diagram</span></div><pre class=\"flowchart-pre\">flowchart TD\n    subgraph CoreEngine [Maximo Scripting Engine]\n        DB[(AUTOSCRIPT Table)] --&gt; ScriptCache[ScriptCacheImpl.java]\n        ScriptCache --&gt; Driver[JSR223ScriptDriver.java]\n        Driver --&gt; CacheMap[(invocableScriptCache)]\n    end</p>\n<p>subgraph MIF_Pipeline [MIF Invocations]\n        PC[Publish Channel / ES / IC] --&gt; Exits[ScriptExternalExit / ScriptUserExit]\n        MOS[Object Structure Engine] --&gt; MOSProcess[MosProcessImpl / MosDefinitionImpl]\n        EndPoint[EndPoint Handler] --&gt; Router[ScriptRouterHandler]\n    end</p>\n<p>Exits --&gt;|invokeFunction| Driver\n    MOSProcess --&gt;|invokeFunction| Driver\n    Router --&gt;|invokeFunction| Driver</pre></div></p>\n</section>"
  },
  "mif-naming": {
    "id": "mif-naming",
    "title": "7.2: Script Naming Conventions & Launch Point Mapping",
    "subtitle": "Complete naming rules and directory mapping evaluated by AutoScript.java.",
    "html": "<h1>7.2: Script Naming Conventions & Launch Point Mapping</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">Complete naming rules and directory mapping evaluated by AutoScript.java.</p>\n<section>\n<p>MIF automation scripts do not rely on standard event-driven MBO launch points. Instead, Maximo identifies them using strict naming conventions evaluated by AutoScript.java:</p>\n<table class=\"ibm-data-table\">\n<thead><tr>\n<th>Integration Component</th>\n<th>Direction / Type</th>\n<th>Script Naming Format</th>\n<th>Concrete Example</th>\n</tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Object Structure (OS)</strong></td>\n<td>Inbound Data Processing</td>\n<td><code>OSIN.<OBJECTSTRUCTURE_NAME></code></td>\n<td><code>OSIN.MXWO</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Object Structure (OS)</strong></td>\n<td>Outbound Data Processing</td>\n<td><code>OSOUT.<OBJECTSTRUCTURE_NAME></code></td>\n<td><code>OSOUT.MXWO</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Object Structure (OS)</strong></td>\n<td>Custom Dynamic Query</td>\n<td><code>OSQUERY.<OS_NAME>.<QUERYNAME></code></td>\n<td><code>OSQUERY.MXPERSON.FINDEMP</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Object Structure (OS)</strong></td>\n<td>Custom Action / RPC</td>\n<td><code>OSACTION.<OS_NAME>.<ACTIONNAME></code></td>\n<td><code>OSACTION.MXWO.CHANGESTATUS</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Publish Channel (PC)</strong></td>\n<td>External Exit</td>\n<td><code>PUBLISH.<CHANNEL_NAME>.EXTEXIT.OUT</code></td>\n<td><code>PUBLISH.MYWOEXP.EXTEXIT.OUT</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Publish Channel (PC)</strong></td>\n<td>User Exit (Before Rules)</td>\n<td><code>PUBLISH.<CHANNEL_NAME>.USEREXIT.OUT.BEFORE</code></td>\n<td><code>PUBLISH.MYWOEXP.USEREXIT.OUT.BEFORE</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Publish Channel (PC)</strong></td>\n<td>User Exit (After Rules)</td>\n<td><code>PUBLISH.<CHANNEL_NAME>.USEREXIT.OUT.AFTER</code></td>\n<td><code>PUBLISH.MYWOEXP.USEREXIT.OUT.AFTER</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Publish Channel (PC)</strong></td>\n<td>Event Filter</td>\n<td><code>PUBLISH.<CHANNEL_NAME>.EVENTFILTER</code></td>\n<td><code>PUBLISH.MYWOEXP.EVENTFILTER</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Enterprise Service (ES)</strong></td>\n<td>External Exit</td>\n<td><code><MESSAGETYPE>.<ES_NAME>.EXTEXIT.IN</code></td>\n<td><code>SYNC.MYWOIN.EXTEXIT.IN</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Enterprise Service (ES)</strong></td>\n<td>User Exit (Before Rules)</td>\n<td><code><MESSAGETYPE>.<ES_NAME>.USEREXIT.IN.BEFORE</code></td>\n<td><code>SYNC.MYWOIN.USEREXIT.IN.BEFORE</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Enterprise Service (ES)</strong></td>\n<td>User Exit (After Rules)</td>\n<td><code><MESSAGETYPE>.<ES_NAME>.USEREXIT.IN.AFTER</code></td>\n<td><code>SYNC.MYWOIN.USEREXIT.IN.AFTER</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Enterprise Service (ES)</strong></td>\n<td>User Exit (MBO Level)</td>\n<td><code><MESSAGETYPE>.<ES_NAME>.USEREXIT.IN.MBO</code></td>\n<td><code>SYNC.MYWOIN.USEREXIT.IN.MBO</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Invoke Channel (IC)</strong></td>\n<td>External Exit (Out/In)</td>\n<td><code>INVOKE.<IC_NAME>.EXTEXIT.<OUT\\</td>\n<td>IN></code></td>\n<td><code>INVOKE.WEATHER_IC.EXTEXIT.OUT</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Invoke Channel (IC)</strong></td>\n<td>User Exit (Out/In)</td>\n<td><code>INVOKE.<IC_NAME>.USEREXIT.<OUT\\</td>\n<td>IN>.<BEFORE\\</td>\n<td>AFTER></code></td>\n<td><code>INVOKE.WEATHER_IC.USEREXIT.OUT.BEFORE</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>End Point / Router</strong></td>\n<td>SCRIPT Handler</td>\n<td>Defined in End Point property <code>SCRIPT</code></td>\n<td><code>SEND_TO_REST_API</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</section>",
    "title_hi": "7.2: Script Naming Conventions (Launch Points Aur Naam Rakhne Ka Tareeqa)",
    "subtitle_hi": "Object Structures, Exits, Event Filters aur Routers ke naming rules.",
    "html_hi": "<h1>7.2: Script Naming Conventions (Launch Points Aur Naam Rakhne Ka Tareeqa)</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">Object Structures, Exits, Event Filters aur Routers ke naming rules.</p>\n<section>\n<p>MIF scripts ka koi alag se launch point MBO nahi hota, balki script ka naam ek predefined pattern par hona chahiye jise AutoScript.java identify karta hai:</p>\n<table class=\"ibm-data-table\">\n<thead><tr>\n<th>Integration Type</th>\n<th>Direction / Exit</th>\n<th>Script Naming Format</th>\n<th>Real Example</th>\n</tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Object Structure (OS)</strong></td>\n<td>Inbound (Aane wala data)</td>\n<td><code>OSIN.<OBJECTSTRUCTURE_NAME></code></td>\n<td><code>OSIN.MXWO</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Object Structure (OS)</strong></td>\n<td>Outbound (Jane wala data)</td>\n<td><code>OSOUT.<OBJECTSTRUCTURE_NAME></code></td>\n<td><code>OSOUT.MXWO</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Object Structure (OS)</strong></td>\n<td>Custom Query</td>\n<td><code>OSQUERY.<OS_NAME>.<QUERYNAME></code></td>\n<td><code>OSQUERY.MXPERSON.FINDEMP</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Object Structure (OS)</strong></td>\n<td>Custom Action</td>\n<td><code>OSACTION.<OS_NAME>.<ACTIONNAME></code></td>\n<td><code>OSACTION.MXWO.CHANGESTATUS</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Publish Channel (PC)</strong></td>\n<td>External Exit</td>\n<td><code>PUBLISH.<CHANNEL_NAME>.EXTEXIT.OUT</code></td>\n<td><code>PUBLISH.MYWOEXP.EXTEXIT.OUT</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Publish Channel (PC)</strong></td>\n<td>User Exit (Before Rules)</td>\n<td><code>PUBLISH.<CHANNEL_NAME>.USEREXIT.OUT.BEFORE</code></td>\n<td><code>PUBLISH.MYWOEXP.USEREXIT.OUT.BEFORE</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Publish Channel (PC)</strong></td>\n<td>User Exit (After Rules)</td>\n<td><code>PUBLISH.<CHANNEL_NAME>.USEREXIT.OUT.AFTER</code></td>\n<td><code>PUBLISH.MYWOEXP.USEREXIT.OUT.AFTER</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Publish Channel (PC)</strong></td>\n<td>Event Filter</td>\n<td><code>PUBLISH.<CHANNEL_NAME>.EVENTFILTER</code></td>\n<td><code>PUBLISH.MYWOEXP.EVENTFILTER</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Enterprise Service (ES)</strong></td>\n<td>External Exit</td>\n<td><code><MESSAGETYPE>.<ES_NAME>.EXTEXIT.IN</code></td>\n<td><code>SYNC.MYWOIN.EXTEXIT.IN</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Enterprise Service (ES)</strong></td>\n<td>User Exit (Before Rules)</td>\n<td><code><MESSAGETYPE>.<ES_NAME>.USEREXIT.IN.BEFORE</code></td>\n<td><code>SYNC.MYWOIN.USEREXIT.IN.BEFORE</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Enterprise Service (ES)</strong></td>\n<td>User Exit (After Rules)</td>\n<td><code><MESSAGETYPE>.<ES_NAME>.USEREXIT.IN.AFTER</code></td>\n<td><code>SYNC.MYWOIN.USEREXIT.IN.AFTER</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Enterprise Service (ES)</strong></td>\n<td>User Exit (MBO Level)</td>\n<td><code><MESSAGETYPE>.<ES_NAME>.USEREXIT.IN.MBO</code></td>\n<td><code>SYNC.MYWOIN.USEREXIT.IN.MBO</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Invoke Channel (IC)</strong></td>\n<td>External Exit (Request/Response)</td>\n<td><code>INVOKE.<IC_NAME>.EXTEXIT.<OUT\\</td>\n<td>IN></code></td>\n<td><code>INVOKE.WEATHER_IC.EXTEXIT.OUT</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Invoke Channel (IC)</strong></td>\n<td>User Exit (Request/Response)</td>\n<td><code>INVOKE.<IC_NAME>.USEREXIT.<OUT\\</td>\n<td>IN>.<BEFORE\\</td>\n<td>AFTER></code></td>\n<td><code>INVOKE.WEATHER_IC.USEREXIT.OUT.BEFORE</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Router / EndPoint</strong></td>\n<td>SCRIPT Handler</td>\n<td>EndPoint ki property me jo <code>SCRIPT</code> naam diya ho</td>\n<td><code>SEND_TO_REST_API</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</section>"
  },
  "mif-osin": {
    "id": "mif-osin",
    "title": "7.3: Inbound Object Structure Scripts (OSIN.<OSNAME>)",
    "subtitle": "8 lifecycle callback hooks and OSProcessScriptContext (ctx) API methods.",
    "html": "<h1>7.3: Inbound Object Structure Scripts (OSIN.<OSNAME>)</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">8 lifecycle callback hooks and OSProcessScriptContext (ctx) API methods.</p>\n<section>\n<p>When data enters Maximo via REST API, OSLC, Enterprise Services, or Interface Tables, MosProcessImpl.java orchestrates inbound message processing across 8 lifecycle callback hooks.</p>\n<h3>Inbound Lifecycle Execution Pipeline</h3>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\"><div class=\"ibm-code-header\"><span>Architecture Flowchart / Diagram</span></div><pre class=\"flowchart-pre\">flowchart TD\n    A[Inbound Message Received] --&gt; B[&quot;1. beforeProcess(ctx)&quot;]\n    B --&gt; C[&quot;2. beforeCreateMboSet(ctx)&quot;]\n    C --&gt; D[&quot;3. afterCreateMboSet(ctx)&quot;]\n    D --&gt; E[&quot;4. mboRules(ctx)&quot;]\n    E --&gt; F[&quot;5. beforeMboData(ctx)&quot;]\n    F --&gt; G[Maximo sets XML/JSON data in MBO]\n    G --&gt; H[&quot;6. afterMboData(ctx)&quot;]\n    H --&gt; I[&quot;7. preSaveRules(ctx)&quot;]\n    I --&gt; J[(Database Commit)]\n    J --&gt; K[&quot;8. afterProcess(ctx)&quot;]</pre></div>\n<h3>Detailed Hook Descriptions:</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>beforeProcess(ctx)</code></strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Executes once at the very beginning of message processing.</li>\n<li>Ideal for global pre-validations and setting message-level transaction flags.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>beforeCreateMboSet(ctx)</code></strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Fires before Maximo creates/fetches the <code>MboSet</code> for a specific Object Structure node.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>afterCreateMboSet(ctx)</code></strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Fires immediately after the <code>MboSet</code> has been instantiated.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>mboRules(ctx)</code></strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Determines how Maximo matches an incoming record to an existing record in the database. Custom record resolution logic is implemented here.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>beforeMboData(ctx)</code></strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Executes right before incoming payload values are transferred into MBO attributes.</li>\n<li>Best place to sanitize, format, or set default field values in the payload structure.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>afterMboData(ctx)</code></strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Executes after field values have been populated into the MBO.</li>\n<li>Ideal for triggering MBO calculations, validations, or dependent attribute assignments.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>preSaveRules(ctx)</code></strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Executes immediately prior to database commit.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>afterProcess(ctx)</code></strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Executes once the entire message and all child MBOs are successfully saved.</li>\n<p></ul>\n<h3><code>OSProcessScriptContext</code> (<code>ctx</code>) API Methods</h3></p>\n<p>The <code>ctx</code> parameter is an instance of OSProcessScriptContext.java:</p>\n<table class=\"ibm-data-table\">\n<thead><tr>\n<th>Method</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ctx.getMbo()</code></td>\n<td>Returns the current MBO being processed.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ctx.getPrimaryMbo()</code></td>\n<td>Returns the root (primary) MBO of the Object Structure.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ctx.getParentMbo()</code></td>\n<td>Returns the immediate parent MBO in the hierarchy.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ctx.getMboSet()</code></td>\n<td>Returns the <code>MboSetRemote</code> associated with the current MBO.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ctx.getData()</code></td>\n<td>Returns the StructureData for the current XML/JSON node.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ctx.isPrimary()</code></td>\n<td>Returns <code>True</code> if the current node is the root object.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ctx.processAsAdd()</code></td>\n<td>Forces the transaction into <strong>Insert (ADD)</strong> mode.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ctx.processAsUpdate()</code></td>\n<td>Forces the transaction into <strong>Update</strong> mode.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ctx.skipMbo()</code></td>\n<td>Skips the current child record (will not insert/update).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ctx.skipTxn()</code></td>\n<td>Discards the entire transaction silently without error.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ctx.skipMboValidate()</code></td>\n<td>Bypasses standard Maximo MBO validation rules.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h3>Production Jython Example (<code>OSIN.MXWO</code>):</h3>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>Jython (Python)</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre># Script Name: OSIN.MXWO\n# Language: Jython (Python)\n<p>def beforeProcess(ctx):\n    service.log_info(&quot;--&gt; Starting Inbound OSIN.MXWO Processing&quot;)</p>\n<p>def beforeMboData(ctx):\n    # Read and sanitize StructureData from incoming payload\n    struc = ctx.getData()\n    if not struc.isCurrentDataNull(&quot;VENDOR&quot;):\n        vendor = struc.getCurrentData(&quot;VENDOR&quot;)\n        struc.setCurrentData(&quot;VENDOR&quot;, vendor.strip().upper())</p>\n<p>def afterMboData(ctx):\n    mbo = ctx.getMbo()\n    \n    # Process primary Work Order attributes\n    if ctx.isPrimary():\n        if mbo.isNull(&quot;DESCRIPTION&quot;):\n            mbo.setValue(&quot;DESCRIPTION&quot;, &quot;Auto-generated via Inbound Integration&quot;, 11L)\n            \n        if mbo.getString(&quot;STATUS&quot;) == &quot;WAPPR&quot;:\n            service.log_info(&quot;Workorder &quot; + mbo.getString(&quot;WONUM&quot;) + &quot; is in WAPPR state.&quot;)</p>\n<p>def preSaveRules(ctx):\n    mbo = ctx.getPrimaryMbo()\n    service.log_info(&quot;Ready to commit WorkOrder: &quot; + mbo.getString(&quot;WONUM&quot;))</p>\n<p>def afterProcess(ctx):\n    service.log_info(&quot;--&gt; Successfully completed OSIN.MXWO transaction&quot;)</pre>\n</div></p>\n</section>",
    "title_hi": "7.3: Inbound Object Structure Scripts (OSIN.<OSNAME>)",
    "subtitle_hi": "8 lifecycle callback hooks aur OSProcessScriptContext (ctx) API ka complete practical guide.",
    "html_hi": "<h1>7.3: Inbound Object Structure Scripts (OSIN.<OSNAME>)</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">8 lifecycle callback hooks aur OSProcessScriptContext (ctx) API ka complete practical guide.</p>\n<section>\n<p>Jab koi data Maximo me REST API, OSLC, Enterprise Service ya Interface Tables ke through andar aata hai, toh MosProcessImpl.java execute hota hai.</p>\n<h3>Inbound Lifecycle Execution Flow</h3>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\"><div class=\"ibm-code-header\"><span>Architecture Flowchart / Diagram</span></div><pre class=\"flowchart-pre\">flowchart TD\n    A[Incoming Message Start] --&gt; B[&quot;1. beforeProcess(ctx)&quot;]\n    B --&gt; C[&quot;2. beforeCreateMboSet(ctx)&quot;]\n    C --&gt; D[&quot;3. afterCreateMboSet(ctx)&quot;]\n    D --&gt; E[&quot;4. mboRules(ctx)&quot;]\n    E --&gt; F[&quot;5. beforeMboData(ctx)&quot;]\n    F --&gt; G[Maximo sets XML/JSON data in MBO]\n    G --&gt; H[&quot;6. afterMboData(ctx)&quot;]\n    H --&gt; I[&quot;7. preSaveRules(ctx)&quot;]\n    I --&gt; J[Save to Database]\n    J --&gt; K[&quot;8. afterProcess(ctx)&quot;]</pre></div>\n<h3>Har Hook Ka Detail Description:</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>beforeProcess(ctx)</code></strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Poori message processing shuru hone se pehle ek baar chalta hai.</li>\n<li>Global validations ya transaction-level settings ke liye use hota hai.</li>\n<p></ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>beforeCreateMboSet(ctx)</code></strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Object Structure ke kisi node ke liye <code>MboSet</code> fetch/create karne se pehle chalta hai.</li></p>\n<p></ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>afterCreateMboSet(ctx)</code></strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li><code>MboSet</code> banne ke baad chalta hai.</li></p>\n<p></ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>mboRules(ctx)</code></strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Maximo decide karta hai ki incoming message ko existing record se kaise match karna hai. Custom record search logic yahan likh sakte hain.</li></p>\n<p></ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>beforeMboData(ctx)</code></strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Incoming payload ke field values MBO me set hone se theek pehle chalta hai.</li>\n<li>Agar incoming data ko modify/clean karna ho (jaise uppercase karna ya default value set karna), toh yeh best jagah hai.</li></p>\n<p></ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>afterMboData(ctx)</code></strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Field values MBO me set ho chuki hoti hain.</li>\n<li>Yahan custom MBO business logic ya calculation execute kar sakte hain.</li></p>\n<p></ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>preSaveRules(ctx)</code></strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Database me commit hone se theek pehle chalta hai.</li></p>\n<p></ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>afterProcess(ctx)</code></strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Pura message aur uske saare child MBOs save ho jane ke baad last me chalta hai.</li></p>\n<p></ul>\n<h3><code>OSProcessScriptContext</code> (<code>ctx</code>) Ke Main Methods</h3></p>\n<p><code>ctx</code> object OSProcessScriptContext.java ka instance hota hai:</p>\n<table class=\"ibm-data-table\">\n<thead><tr>\n<th>Method</th>\n<th>Kya Karta Hai?</th>\n</tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ctx.getMbo()</code></td>\n<td>Current processing wala MBO return karta hai.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ctx.getPrimaryMbo()</code></td>\n<td>Root (Main) MBO return karta hai.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ctx.getParentMbo()</code></td>\n<td>Hierarchy me parent MBO return karta hai.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ctx.getMboSet()</code></td>\n<td>Current MBO ka <code>MboSetRemote</code> return karta hai.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ctx.getData()</code></td>\n<td>Current XML/JSON node ka StructureData deta hai.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ctx.isPrimary()</code></td>\n<td>Agar yeh root object hai toh <code>True</code> return karta hai.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ctx.processAsAdd()</code></td>\n<td>Record ko forcibly <strong>New Insert (ADD)</strong> mode me process karta hai.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ctx.processAsUpdate()</code></td>\n<td>Record ko forcibly <strong>Update</strong> mode me process karta hai.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ctx.skipMbo()</code></td>\n<td>Current child record ko skip kar deta hai (insert/update nahi karta).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ctx.skipTxn()</code></td>\n<td>Poori transaction ko bina error ke drop/skip kar deta hai.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ctx.skipMboValidate()</code></td>\n<td>Maximo ki default validation bypass karta hai.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h3>Complete Jython Example (<code>OSIN.MXWO</code>):</h3>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>Jython (Python)</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre># Script Name: OSIN.MXWO\n# Language: Jython\n<p>def beforeProcess(ctx):\n    service.log_info(&quot;--&gt; Starting Inbound OSIN.MXWO Processing&quot;)</p>\n<p>def beforeMboData(ctx):\n    # Incoming payload se StructureData read karna\n    struc = ctx.getData()\n    \n    # Agar VENDOR field me data hai toh usko uppercase convert karo\n    if not struc.isCurrentDataNull(&quot;VENDOR&quot;):\n        vendor = struc.getCurrentData(&quot;VENDOR&quot;)\n        struc.setCurrentData(&quot;VENDOR&quot;, vendor.upper())</p>\n<p>def afterMboData(ctx):\n    mbo = ctx.getMbo()\n    \n    # Agar primary work order hai aur description khali hai\n    if ctx.isPrimary():\n        if mbo.isNull(&quot;DESCRIPTION&quot;):\n            mbo.setValue(&quot;DESCRIPTION&quot;, &quot;Auto created from Integration&quot;, 11L)\n            \n        # Agar work order status WAPPR hai toh custom logic run karo\n        if mbo.getString(&quot;STATUS&quot;) == &quot;WAPPR&quot;:\n            service.log_info(&quot;Workorder &quot; + mbo.getString(&quot;WONUM&quot;) + &quot; is in WAPPR state.&quot;)</p>\n<p>def preSaveRules(ctx):\n    mbo = ctx.getPrimaryMbo()\n    service.log_info(&quot;Ready to commit WorkOrder: &quot; + mbo.getString(&quot;WONUM&quot;))</p>\n<p>def afterProcess(ctx):\n    service.log_info(&quot;--&gt; Successfully completed OSIN.MXWO message!&quot;)</pre>\n</div></p>\n</section>"
  },
  "mif-osout": {
    "id": "mif-osout",
    "title": "7.4: Outbound Object Structure Scripts (OSOUT.<OSNAME>)",
    "subtitle": "Controlling outbound serialization with skipMbo, overrideValues, and skipCols.",
    "html": "<h1>7.4: Outbound Object Structure Scripts (OSOUT.<OSNAME>)</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">Controlling outbound serialization with skipMbo, overrideValues, and skipCols.</p>\n<section>\n<p>When data is exported from Maximo (via Publish Channel, REST API GET, or OSLC Export), MosDefinitionImpl.java orchestrates outbound serialization.</p>\n<h3>Outbound Callback Methods:</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>skipMbo(ctx)</code></strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Determines whether an individual MBO should be included in the outgoing message.</li>\n<li><code>ctx.skipMbo()</code> excludes the specific MBO.</li>\n<li><code>ctx.skipTxn()</code> suppresses the entire outbound transaction.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>overrideValues(ctx)</code></strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Dynamically modifies attribute values in the outgoing XML/JSON payload using <code>ctx.overrideColValue(colName, value)</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>skipCols(ctx)</code></strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Suppresses sensitive or unnecessary attributes from the output payload using <code>ctx.skipCol(colName)</code>.</li>\n<p></ul>\n<h3>Production Jython Example (<code>OSOUT.MXWO</code>):</h3></p>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>Jython (Python)</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre># Script Name: OSOUT.MXWO\n# Language: Jython (Python)\n<p>def skipMbo(ctx):\n    mbo = ctx.getMbo()\n    # Suppress historic records from export\n    if mbo.getBoolean(&quot;HISTORYFLAG&quot;):\n        ctx.skipMbo()</p>\n<p>def overrideValues(ctx):\n    mbo = ctx.getMbo()\n    if ctx.getMosDetailInfo().getObjectName() == &quot;WORKORDER&quot;:\n        desc = mbo.getString(&quot;DESCRIPTION&quot;)\n        ctx.overrideColValue(&quot;DESCRIPTION&quot;, &quot;EXPORTED: &quot; + desc)</p>\n<p>def skipCols(ctx):\n    # Omit internal auditing identifiers\n    ctx.skipCol(&quot;SENDERSYSID&quot;)\n    ctx.skipCol(&quot;SOURCESYSID&quot;)</pre>\n</div></p>\n</section>",
    "title_hi": "7.4: Outbound Object Structure Scripts (OSOUT.<OSNAME>)",
    "subtitle_hi": "skipMbo, overrideValues, aur skipCols se outgoing data modify aur filter karna.",
    "html_hi": "<h1>7.4: Outbound Object Structure Scripts (OSOUT.<OSNAME>)</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">skipMbo, overrideValues, aur skipCols se outgoing data modify aur filter karna.</p>\n<section>\n<p>Jab Maximo se data bahar export ho raha hota hai (Publish Channel, REST API GET, OSLC Export), tab MosDefinitionImpl.java execute hota hai.</p>\n<h3>Outbound Callback Functions:</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>skipMbo(ctx)</code></strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Decide karta hai ki kisi MBO record ko export me bhejna hai ya nahi.</li>\n<li><code>ctx.skipMbo()</code> call karne se woh particular MBO XML/JSON me nahi jayega.</li>\n<li><code>ctx.skipTxn()</code> call karne se pura message hi export nahi hoga.</li>\n<p></ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>overrideValues(ctx)</code></strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Outbound XML/JSON me kisi attribute ki value dynamically change/override karne ke liye.</li>\n<li><code>ctx.overrideColValue(colName, value)</code> use karte hain.</li></p>\n<p></ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>skipCols(ctx)</code></strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Kisi specific attribute/column ko outgoing payload se hide/remove karne ke liye.</li>\n<li><code>ctx.skipCol(colName)</code> use karte hain.</li></p>\n<p></ul>\n<h3>Complete Jython Example (<code>OSOUT.MXWO</code>):</h3></p>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>Jython (Python)</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre># Script Name: OSOUT.MXWO\n# Language: Jython\n<p>def skipMbo(ctx):\n    mbo = ctx.getMbo()\n    # Agar Work Order history me chala gaya hai toh export mat karo\n    if mbo.getBoolean(&quot;HISTORYFLAG&quot;) == True:\n        ctx.skipMbo()</p>\n<p>def overrideValues(ctx):\n    mbo = ctx.getMbo()\n    # Outbound XML me description ke aage prefix laga do\n    if ctx.getMosDetailInfo().getObjectName() == &quot;WORKORDER&quot;:\n        desc = mbo.getString(&quot;DESCRIPTION&quot;)\n        ctx.overrideColValue(&quot;DESCRIPTION&quot;, &quot;EXPORTED: &quot; + desc)</p>\n<p>def skipCols(ctx):\n    # Sensitive ya internal columns ko hide karo\n    ctx.skipCol(&quot;SENDERSYSID&quot;)\n    ctx.skipCol(&quot;SOURCESYSID&quot;)</pre>\n</div></p>\n</section>"
  },
  "mif-osquery-osaction": {
    "id": "mif-osquery-osaction",
    "title": "7.5: Dynamic Query & Custom Action Scripts (OSQUERY & OSACTION)",
    "subtitle": "Dynamic REST query filtering and RPC business methods on Maximo Object Structures.",
    "html": "<h1>7.5: Dynamic Query & Custom Action Scripts (OSQUERY & OSACTION)</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">Dynamic REST query filtering and RPC business methods on Maximo Object Structures.</p>\n<section>\n<p>Maximo Next-Gen REST/JSON APIs and OSLC support <strong>Dynamic Query Filtering</strong> and <strong>Custom Remote Procedure Calls (RPC)</strong> on Object Structures using <code>OSQUERY</code> and <code>OSACTION</code> scripts.</p>\n<div class=\"ibm-callout ibm-callout-info\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-callout-title\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-info\"></i> Note</div>\n  <div class=\"ibm-callout-content\"><p>Unlike <code>OSIN</code> and <code>OSOUT</code> (which use <code>INTERFACE = 1</code> callback functions), <code>OSQUERY</code> and <code>OSACTION</code> scripts run with <code>INTERFACE = 0</code> as top-to-bottom procedural scripts.</p></div>\n</div>\n<h3>A. Custom Query Scripts (<code>OSQUERY.<OSNAME>.<QUERYNAME></code>)</h3>\n<h4>Problem Solved</h4>\nStandard REST APIs rely on static <code>oslc.where</code> filters (e.g. <code>oslc.where=status='APPR'</code>). However:\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Dynamic Parameter Combinations</strong>: External clients often pass arbitrary combinations of URL parameters (e.g. <code>siteid + mincost + date_range</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Security & Encapsulation</strong>: External callers should not be exposed to internal database schema or permitted to construct direct SQL where clauses.</li>\n<li><strong>Complex Relational Logic</strong>: Filtering parent records based on complex child/subquery conditions (e.g. Work Orders having labor transactions for specific crafts).</li>\n<p></ol>\n\ud83d\udc49 <strong><code>OSQUERY</code> reads dynamic URL parameters at runtime and applies targeted SQL where clauses or QBE filters directly to the <code>MboSet</code>.</strong></p>\n<h4>Architecture & Execution Flow</h4>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\"><div class=\"ibm-code-header\"><span>Architecture Flowchart / Diagram</span></div><pre class=\"flowchart-pre\">sequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    actor Client as External Client / Mobile App\n    participant REST as Maximo OSLC REST Engine\n    participant Java as SavedQueryHandler.java\n    participant Script as OSQUERY.MXWO.ADVSEARCH\n    participant DB as Maximo Database\n<p>Client-&gt;&gt;REST: GET /maximo/oslc/os/mxwo?savedQuery=ADVSEARCH&amp;siteid=BEDFORD&amp;mincost=5000&amp;days=7\n    REST-&gt;&gt;Java: Route request to SavedQueryHandler\n    Java-&gt;&gt;Java: 1. Extract query params into &#x27;context&#x27; map&lt;br/&gt;2. Bind target &#x27;mboset&#x27;&lt;br/&gt;3. Inject script parameters\n    Java-&gt;&gt;Script: Execute OSQUERY.MXWO.ADVSEARCH\n    Script-&gt;&gt;Script: 1. Read parameters from context&lt;br/&gt;2. Build SQL condition&lt;br/&gt;3. mboset.setWhere(where_clause)\n    Script-&gt;&gt;Java: Return control\n    Java-&gt;&gt;DB: Fetch matching records from mboset\n    Java-&gt;&gt;Client: HTTP 200 OK + Paginated JSON Array</pre></div></p>\n<h4>Maximo UI Setup Steps:</h4>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Register Query in Object Structures App</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Open <strong>Object Structures</strong> application (<code>MXWO</code>).</li>\n<li>Select Action $\\rightarrow$ <strong>Add/Modify OSLC Queries</strong>.</li>\n<li>Create New Row:</li>\n<li><strong>Query Clause Name</strong>: <code>ADVSEARCH</code> (Matches URL query <code>savedQuery=ADVSEARCH</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Script Name</strong>: <code>OSQUERY.MXWO.ADVSEARCH</code> (FldScriptnameOslcQuery.java).</li>\n<li><strong>Public</strong>: Checked.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Create Script in Automation Scripts App</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Select <strong>Create</strong> $\\rightarrow$ <strong>Script for Integration</strong>.</li>\n<li>Direction: <code>OSQUERY</code>, Object Structure: <code>MXWO</code>, Query Name: <code>ADVSEARCH</code>.</li>\n<li>Script Name auto-populates as <code>OSQUERY.MXWO.ADVSEARCH</code>.</li>\n<li>Language: <code>python</code> (Jython). Save & Activate.</li>\n<p></ul>\n<h4>Injected Variables (SavedQueryHandler.java):</h4></p>\n<table class=\"ibm-data-table\">\n<thead><tr>\n<th>Variable Name</th>\n<th>Java Type</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>mboset</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>psdi.mbo.MboSetRemote</code></td>\n<td>Target root <code>MboSet</code> to which <code>setWhere(...)</code> or <code>setQbe(...)</code> is applied.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>context</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>java.util.Map<String, Object></code></td>\n<td>Map containing all parsed URL query parameters.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code><paramName></code></strong></td>\n<td>String / Object</td>\n<td>Query parameters accessible directly or via <code>context.get(\"paramName\")</code>.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>service</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>ScriptService</code></td>\n<td>Helper object for logging and DB operations.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h4>Production Jython Example (<code>OSQUERY.MXWO.ADVSEARCH</code>):</h4>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>Jython (Python)</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre># Script Name: OSQUERY.MXWO.ADVSEARCH\n# Language: Jython (Python)\n# URL: GET /maximo/oslc/os/mxwo?savedQuery=ADVSEARCH&amp;siteid=BEDFORD&amp;mincost=2000&amp;status=APPR,INPRG&amp;days=30\n<p>import java.util.Calendar\nimport java.text.SimpleDateFormat</p>\n<p># 1. Extract query parameters safely\ntarget_site = context.get(&quot;siteid&quot;)\nmin_cost = context.get(&quot;mincost&quot;)\nstatus_list = context.get(&quot;status&quot;)\ndays_ago = context.get(&quot;days&quot;)</p>\n<p>service.log_info(&quot;--&gt; Executing OSQUERY.MXWO.ADVSEARCH&quot;)</p>\n<p># 2. Build dynamic SQL criteria\nwhere_clause = &quot;historyflag = 0 and istask = 0&quot;</p>\n<p>if target_site is not None and str(target_site).strip() != &quot;&quot;:\n    where_clause += &quot; and siteid = &#x27;&quot; + str(target_site).replace(&quot;&#x27;&quot;, &quot;&#x27;&#x27;&quot;) + &quot;&#x27;&quot;</p>\n<p>if min_cost is not None and str(min_cost).strip() != &quot;&quot;:\n    where_clause += &quot; and acttotalcost &gt;= &quot; + str(min_cost)</p>\n<p>if status_list is not None and str(status_list).strip() != &quot;&quot;:\n    statuses = str(status_list).split(&quot;,&quot;)\n    formatted = &quot;, &quot;.join([&quot;&#x27;&quot; + s.strip().replace(&quot;&#x27;&quot;, &quot;&#x27;&#x27;&quot;) + &quot;&#x27;&quot; for s in statuses])\n    where_clause += &quot; and status in (&quot; + formatted + &quot;)&quot;</p>\n<p>if days_ago is not None and str(days_ago).isdigit():\n    cal = java.util.Calendar.getInstance()\n    cal.add(java.util.Calendar.DAY_OF_MONTH, -int(days_ago))\n    sdf = java.text.SimpleDateFormat(&quot;yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss&quot;)\n    date_str = sdf.format(cal.getTime())\n    where_clause += &quot; and reportdate &gt;= to_date(&#x27;&quot; + date_str + &quot;&#x27;, &#x27;YYYY-MM-DD HH24:MI:SS&#x27;)&quot;</p>\n<p># 3. Apply where clause to target MboSet\nmboset.setWhere(where_clause)\nservice.log_info(&quot;Applied dynamic where clause: &quot; + where_clause)</pre>\n</div></p>\n<h3>B. Custom Action Scripts (<code>OSACTION.<OSNAME>.<ACTIONNAME></code>)</h3>\n<h4>Problem Solved</h4>\nStandard REST APIs perform CRUD operations (updating database columns). However, external callers often need to trigger <strong>Business Methods / Remote Procedures (RPC)</strong>:\n<ul>\n<li>Changing Work Order status (<code>mbo.changeStatus()</code>) with validation and approval memos.</li>\n<li>Approving Purchase Orders through enterprise workflows.</li>\n<li>Creating actual labor entries while updating parent record state.</li>\n<p></ul>\n\ud83d\udc49 <strong><code>OSACTION</code> exposes custom business methods as REST endpoints.</strong></p>\n<h4>Architecture & Execution Flow</h4>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\"><div class=\"ibm-code-header\"><span>Architecture Flowchart / Diagram</span></div><pre class=\"flowchart-pre\">sequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    actor Client as External Client / Mobile App\n    participant REST as Maximo OSLC REST Engine\n    participant Java as ScriptActionHandler.java\n    participant Script as OSACTION.MXWO.CHANGESTATUS\n    participant DB as Maximo Database\n<p>Client-&gt;&gt;REST: POST /maximo/oslc/os/mxwo/1234?action=CHANGESTATUS&lt;br/&gt;Body: {&quot;newstatus&quot;: &quot;COMP&quot;, &quot;memo&quot;: &quot;Done&quot;, &quot;laborhours&quot;: 3.5}\n    REST-&gt;&gt;Java: Route request to ScriptActionHandler\n    Java-&gt;&gt;Java: 1. Load MBO (WO 1234)&lt;br/&gt;2. Decode body into &#x27;requestBody&#x27;&lt;br/&gt;3. Inject variables (mbo, request, service)\n    Java-&gt;&gt;Script: Execute OSACTION.MXWO.CHANGESTATUS\n    Script-&gt;&gt;Script: 1. mbo.changeStatus(&quot;COMP&quot;, ...)&lt;br/&gt;2. Add child record in LABTRANS&lt;br/&gt;3. Set responseBody JSON\n    Script-&gt;&gt;Java: Return responseBody\n    Java-&gt;&gt;DB: mbo.getThisMboSet().save() (Automatic Commit)\n    Java-&gt;&gt;Client: HTTP 200 OK + JSON Response</pre></div></p>\n<h4>Injected Variables (ScriptActionHandler.java):</h4>\n<table class=\"ibm-data-table\">\n<thead><tr>\n<th>Variable Name</th>\n<th>Java Type</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>mbo</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>psdi.mbo.MboRemote</code></td>\n<td>Target MBO instance (when invoked on a single resource URL).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>mboset</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>psdi.mbo.MboSetRemote</code></td>\n<td>Target <code>MboSet</code> (when invoked at the collection level).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>requestBody</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>java.lang.String</code></td>\n<td>Incoming HTTP request body (JSON/XML string).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>responseBody</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>java.lang.Object</code> <em>(Out)</em></td>\n<td>Custom return payload (JSON string or byte array) sent back to the client.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>request</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>OslcRequest</code></td>\n<td>HTTP request details (headers, parameters, URI).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>responseHeaders</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>Map<String, String></code></td>\n<td>HTTP response headers.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>userInfo</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>UserInfo</code></td>\n<td>Current session user details.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>service</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>ScriptService</code></td>\n<td>Helper object for logging and error throwing.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h4>Production Jython Example (<code>OSACTION.MXWO.CHANGESTATUS</code>):</h4>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>Jython (Python)</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre># Script Name: OSACTION.MXWO.CHANGESTATUS\n# Language: Jython (Python)\n# Trigger: POST /maximo/oslc/os/mxwo/54321?action=CHANGESTATUS\n# Body: {&quot;newstatus&quot;: &quot;COMP&quot;, &quot;memo&quot;: &quot;Motor replaced and tested&quot;, &quot;laborhours&quot;: 3.5}\n<p>import java.util.Date</p>\n<p># 1. Parse incoming request body\nif requestBody is not None:\n    req_json = service.tojsonobject(requestBody)\n    target_status = req_json.get(&quot;newstatus&quot;)\n    status_memo = req_json.get(&quot;memo&quot;)\n    actual_hours = req_json.get(&quot;laborhours&quot;)\nelse:\n    target_status = None\n    status_memo = &quot;Updated via Integration Action&quot;\n    actual_hours = 0.0</p>\n<p># 2. Validations\nif mbo is None:\n    service.error(&quot;workorder&quot;, &quot;noworkorderfound&quot;)</p>\n<p>if target_status is None:\n    service.error(&quot;workorder&quot;, &quot;nostatusprovided&quot;)</p>\n<p># 3. Execute Maximo MBO business logic\nmbo.changeStatus(target_status, java.util.Date(), status_memo, 11L)</p>\n<p>if actual_hours is not None and float(actual_hours) &gt; 0:\n    labtrans_set = mbo.getMboSet(&quot;LABTRANS&quot;)\n    new_lab = labtrans_set.add()\n    new_lab.setValue(&quot;LABORCODE&quot;, userInfo.getPersonId(), 11L)\n    new_lab.setValue(&quot;REGULARHRS&quot;, float(actual_hours), 11L)\n    new_lab.setValue(&quot;TRANSDATE&quot;, java.util.Date(), 11L)</p>\n<p># 4. Construct custom JSON response (Automatic DB Save will be executed by ScriptActionHandler)\nresp_dict = service.tojsonobject(&quot;{}&quot;)\nresp_dict.put(&quot;result&quot;, &quot;SUCCESS&quot;)\nresp_dict.put(&quot;wonum&quot;, mbo.getString(&quot;WONUM&quot;))\nresp_dict.put(&quot;status&quot;, mbo.getString(&quot;STATUS&quot;))\nresp_dict.put(&quot;updatedBy&quot;, userInfo.getUserName())\nresp_dict.put(&quot;message&quot;, &quot;Work order status successfully changed to &quot; + target_status)</p>\n<p>responseBody = service.jsonToString(resp_dict)</pre>\n</div></p>\n</section>",
    "title_hi": "7.5: Custom Query Aur Action Scripts (OSQUERY & OSACTION)",
    "subtitle_hi": "REST APIs me dynamic where clauses aur business RPC actions run karna.",
    "html_hi": "<h1>7.5: Custom Query Aur Action Scripts (OSQUERY & OSACTION)</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">REST APIs me dynamic where clauses aur business RPC actions run karna.</p>\n<section>\n<p>Maximo Next-Gen REST/JSON APIs aur OSLC ke andar Object Structures par <strong>Custom Dynamic Query Filtering</strong> aur <strong>Custom Business Actions / Remote Procedures</strong> perform karne ke liye <code>OSQUERY</code> aur <code>OSACTION</code> scripts use hoti hain.</p>\n<div class=\"ibm-callout ibm-callout-info\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-callout-title\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-info\"></i> Note</div>\n  <div class=\"ibm-callout-content\"><p><code>OSIN</code> aur <code>OSOUT</code> scripts <code>INTERFACE = 1</code> ke sath function library callbacks use karti hain, jabki <code>OSQUERY</code> aur <code>OSACTION</code> scripts <code>INTERFACE = 0</code> ke sath normal top-to-bottom procedural execution karti hain.</p></div>\n</div>\n<h3>A. Custom Query Scripts (<code>OSQUERY.<OSNAME>.<QUERYNAME></code>)</h3>\n<h4>1. Kyun Use Hota Hai? (Static Saved Queries vs Dynamic REST Queries)</h4>\nMaximo REST API me records fetch karte waqt external systems standard <code>oslc.where</code> parameter bhej sakti hain (e.g. <code>oslc.where=status='APPR'</code>).\n<p>Lekin real-world integration architectures me static where clauses kafi nahi hote:\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Multiple Optional URL Filters</strong>: External client kabhi sirf <code>siteid</code> bhejta hai, kabhi <code>siteid + mincost</code>, aur kabhi <code>siteid + craft + date</code>. Har combination ke liye alag static query nahi banayi ja sakti.</li>\n<li><strong>Security & Abstraction</strong>: External systems ko internal Maximo database tables aur SQL schema ka access ya direct SQL clause likhne ki permission nahi honi chahiye (SQL Injection risk se bachne ke liye).</li>\n<li><strong>Complex Multi-Table / Relationship Logic</strong>: Aisi queries jahan child tables (e.g. LABTRANS, PO, MATUSETRANS) ke data par parent (WORKORDER) filter karna ho ya user-specific dynamic dates calculate karni ho.</li></p>\n<p></ol>\n\ud83d\udc49 <strong><code>OSQUERY</code> ka kaam hai:</strong> External REST API se aane wale dynamic URL parameters ko padh kar runtime par target <code>MboSet</code> par <strong>Custom Dynamic SQL ya QBE Filter</strong> apply karna!</p>\n<h4>2. Execution Architecture & Sequence Flow:</h4>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\"><div class=\"ibm-code-header\"><span>Architecture Flowchart / Diagram</span></div><pre class=\"flowchart-pre\">sequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    actor Client as External Client / Mobile App\n    participant REST as Maximo OSLC REST Engine\n    participant Java as SavedQueryHandler.java\n    participant Script as OSQUERY.MXWO.ADVSEARCH\n    participant DB as Maximo Database\n<p>Client-&gt;&gt;REST: GET /maximo/oslc/os/mxwo?savedQuery=ADVSEARCH&amp;siteid=BEDFORD&amp;mincost=5000&amp;days=7\n    REST-&gt;&gt;Java: Match savedQuery &amp; call SavedQueryHandler\n    Java-&gt;&gt;Java: 1. Parse URL query params into &#x27;context&#x27; map&lt;br/&gt;2. Bind target &#x27;mboset&#x27;&lt;br/&gt;3. Inject script parameters\n    Java-&gt;&gt;Script: Execute OSQUERY.MXWO.ADVSEARCH\n    Script-&gt;&gt;Script: 1. Read siteid, mincost, days from context&lt;br/&gt;2. Build dynamic SQL where clause&lt;br/&gt;3. mboset.setWhere(where_clause)\n    Script-&gt;&gt;Java: Return control\n    Java-&gt;&gt;DB: Fetch matching records from mboset\n    Java-&gt;&gt;Client: HTTP 200 OK + Paginated JSON Array of Records</pre></div></p>\n<h4>3. Maximo UI Setup Steps (Step-by-Step):</h4>\n<p>##### Step A: Object Structures App Me Query Register Karein:\n<ol>\n<li>Go to <strong>Object Structures</strong> application (search <code>MXWO</code>).</li>\n<li>Click <strong>More Actions (Select Action)</strong> $\\rightarrow$ <strong>Add/Modify OSLC Queries</strong>.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>New Row</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Query Clause Name</strong>: <code>ADVSEARCH</code> (Client URL me <code>savedQuery=ADVSEARCH</code> bhejega).</li>\n<li><strong>Description</strong>: <code>Dynamic Multi-Parameter Work Order Search</code></li>\n<li><strong>Script Name</strong>: <code>OSQUERY.MXWO.ADVSEARCH</code> (FldScriptnameOslcQuery.java enforces the mandatory <code>OSQUERY.<OSNAME>.<QUERYNAME></code> format).</li>\n<li><strong>Public</strong>: Checkbox ON karein taaki sabhi authorized API clients use kar sakein (ya specific Security Role assign karein).</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li>Click <strong>OK</strong> & Save.</li></p>\n<p></ol>\n##### Step B: Automation Scripts App Me Script Create Karein:\n<ol>\n<li>Go to <strong>Automation Scripts</strong> application.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Create</strong> $\\rightarrow$ <strong>Script for Integration</strong>.</li>\n<li>Select:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Integration Direction</strong>: <code>OSQUERY</code></li>\n<li><strong>Object Structure</strong>: <code>MXWO</code></li>\n<li><strong>Query Name</strong>: <code>ADVSEARCH</code></li>\n<li><strong>Script Name</strong>: Automatically generates <code>OSQUERY.MXWO.ADVSEARCH</code> (AutoScript.java).</li>\n<li><strong>Script Language</strong>: <code>python</code> (Jython).</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li>Paste the query logic and click <strong>Save & Activate</strong>.</li></p>\n<p></ol>\n<h4>4. Injected Implicit Variables (Runtime Context):</h4></p>\n<p>SavedQueryHandler.java runtime par script ke andar ye variables inject karta hai:</p>\n<table class=\"ibm-data-table\">\n<thead><tr>\n<th>Variable Name</th>\n<th>Java Data Type</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>mboset</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>psdi.mbo.MboSetRemote</code></td>\n<td>Target Object Structure ka root <code>MboSet</code> jisme dynamic <code>setWhere(...)</code> ya <code>setQbe(...)</code> lagana hai.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>context</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>java.util.Map<String, Object></code></td>\n<td>Script context map jisme saare URL query parameters mapped hote hain.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code><paramName></code></strong></td>\n<td>String / Object</td>\n<td>URL me bheje gaye query parameters direct variable ke roop me ya <code>context.get(\"paramName\")</code> se access hote hain.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>scriptName</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>java.lang.String</code></td>\n<td>Script identifier (e.g. <code>OSQUERY.MXWO.ADVSEARCH</code>).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>service</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>ScriptService</code></td>\n<td>Helper object (logging, database helper methods, system properties).</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h4>5. Real-World Production Jython Examples:</h4>\n<p>##### Example 1: Dynamic Multi-Criteria Search (<code>OSQUERY.MXWO.ADVSEARCH</code>)\nClient URL: <code>GET /maximo/oslc/os/mxwo?savedQuery=ADVSEARCH&siteid=BEDFORD&mincost=2000&status=APPR,INPRG&days=30</code></p>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>Jython (Python)</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre># Script Name: OSQUERY.MXWO.ADVSEARCH\n# Language: Jython (Python)\n<p>import java.util.Calendar\nimport java.text.SimpleDateFormat</p>\n<p># 1. URL Query Parameters extract karna (safe access via context map)\ntarget_site = context.get(&quot;siteid&quot;)\nmin_cost = context.get(&quot;mincost&quot;)\nstatus_list = context.get(&quot;status&quot;)\ndays_ago = context.get(&quot;days&quot;)</p>\n<p>service.log_info(&quot;--&gt; Running OSQUERY.MXWO.ADVSEARCH&quot;)</p>\n<p># 2. Base SQL condition build karna\nwhere_clause = &quot;historyflag = 0 and istask = 0&quot;</p>\n<p># (a) Site ID filter\nif target_site is not None and str(target_site).strip() != &quot;&quot;:\n    where_clause += &quot; and siteid = &#x27;&quot; + str(target_site).replace(&quot;&#x27;&quot;, &quot;&#x27;&#x27;&quot;) + &quot;&#x27;&quot;</p>\n<p># (b) Minimum Actual Cost filter\nif min_cost is not None and str(min_cost).strip() != &quot;&quot;:\n    where_clause += &quot; and acttotalcost &gt;= &quot; + str(min_cost)</p>\n<p># (c) Comma-separated status list filter (e.g. &quot;APPR,INPRG&quot;)\nif status_list is not None and str(status_list).strip() != &quot;&quot;:\n    statuses = str(status_list).split(&quot;,&quot;)\n    formatted_statuses = &quot;, &quot;.join([&quot;&#x27;&quot; + s.strip().replace(&quot;&#x27;&quot;, &quot;&#x27;&#x27;&quot;) + &quot;&#x27;&quot; for s in statuses])\n    where_clause += &quot; and status in (&quot; + formatted_statuses + &quot;)&quot;</p>\n<p># (d) Dynamic Date Filter (e.g. created in last X days)\nif days_ago is not None and str(days_ago).isdigit():\n    cal = java.util.Calendar.getInstance()\n    cal.add(java.util.Calendar.DAY_OF_MONTH, -int(days_ago))\n    sdf = java.text.SimpleDateFormat(&quot;yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss&quot;)\n    date_str = sdf.format(cal.getTime())\n    where_clause += &quot; and reportdate &gt;= to_date(&#x27;&quot; + date_str + &quot;&#x27;, &#x27;YYYY-MM-DD HH24:MI:SS&#x27;)&quot;</p>\n<p># 3. Target MboSet par dynamic where clause set karna\nmboset.setWhere(where_clause)\nservice.log_info(&quot;OSQUERY successfully applied dynamic where clause: &quot; + where_clause)</pre>\n</div></p>\n<p>##### Example 2: Sub-Table / Child Relationship Filter (<code>OSQUERY.MXWO.BYCRAFT</code>)\nClient URL: <code>GET /maximo/oslc/os/mxwo?savedQuery=BYCRAFT&craft=ELEC&siteid=BEDFORD</code>\n<em>(Un Work Orders ko dhoondhna jinme specific Craft ki labor requirement ya actual labor lagi ho)</em></p>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>Jython (Python)</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre># Script Name: OSQUERY.MXWO.BYCRAFT\n# Language: Jython (Python)\n<p>target_craft = context.get(&quot;craft&quot;)\ntarget_site = context.get(&quot;siteid&quot;)</p>\n<p>where_clause = &quot;historyflag = 0&quot;</p>\n<p>if target_site is not None:\n    where_clause += &quot; and siteid = &#x27;&quot; + str(target_site).replace(&quot;&#x27;&quot;, &quot;&#x27;&#x27;&quot;) + &quot;&#x27;&quot;</p>\n<p># Child LABTRANS subquery lagana\nif target_craft is not None:\n    clean_craft = str(target_craft).replace(&quot;&#x27;&quot;, &quot;&#x27;&#x27;&quot;)\n    where_clause += &quot; and wonum in (select wonum from wplabor where craft = &#x27;&quot; + clean_craft + &quot;&#x27;)&quot;</p>\n<p>mboset.setWhere(where_clause)\nservice.log_info(&quot;OSQUERY applied Craft where clause: &quot; + where_clause)</pre>\n</div></p>\n<h4>6. Important Behind-the-Scenes Behaviors:</h4>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Read-Only Execution (No DB Save)</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n   <code>OSQUERY</code> scripts data read/query karne ke liye hoti hain. Isme database me koi <code>save()</code> ya commit trigger nahi hota.\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Automatic Framework Pagination</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n   Aapko script ke andar pagination logic (limit / offset) likhne ki zaroorat nahi hoti. Maximo OSLC framework standard parameters (jaise <code>oslc.pageSize=50</code>, <code>pageno=2</code>, <code>_dropzero=1</code>) ko script ke filter lagaye gaye <code>mboset</code> par automatically handle kar leta hai.\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>INTERFACE = 0</code> Execution</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n   <code>OSIN</code> aur <code>OSOUT</code> ki tarah isme alag-alag functions nahi hote. Script poori top-to-bottom procedural tareeqe se execute hoti hai.\n<h3>B. Custom Action Scripts (<code>OSACTION.<OSNAME>.<ACTIONNAME></code>)</h3>\n<h4>1. Kyun Use Hota Hai? (Problem It Solves - CRUD vs RPC)</h4>\nStandard Maximo REST APIs me jab koi external client <code>POST</code> ya <code>PATCH</code> call bhejta hai, toh Maximo sirf database columns (fields) update karta hai (e.g. <code>DESCRIPTION = 'Test'</code>).\n<p>Lekin real-world business requirements me external systems (Mobile apps, ServiceNow, SAP, Webhooks) ko sirf column update nahi karna hota, balki Maximo ke <strong>Business Methods / Complex Actions</strong> trigger karne hote hain:\n<ul>\n<li>Work Order ka status change karna (<code>mbo.changeStatus()</code>) aur approval memo record karna.</li>\n<li>Purchase Order ki approval process run karna.</li>\n<li>Meter reading validate karke Actual Labor transactions add karna.</li>\n<li>Ek record se related naya child record create karna.</li></p>\n<p></ul>\nExternal systems direct Maximo ke Java methods nahi chala sakti. <strong><code>OSACTION</code> unke liye REST API ke through Maximo ke andar Custom Method / Remote Procedure Call (RPC) execute karne ka gateway banta hai.</strong></p>\n<h4>2. Execution Architecture & Sequence Flow:</h4>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\"><div class=\"ibm-code-header\"><span>Architecture Flowchart / Diagram</span></div><pre class=\"flowchart-pre\">sequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    actor Client as External Client / Mobile App\n    participant REST as Maximo OSLC REST Engine\n    participant Java as ScriptActionHandler.java\n    participant Script as OSACTION.MXWO.CHANGESTATUS\n    participant DB as Maximo Database\n<p>Client-&gt;&gt;REST: POST /maximo/oslc/os/mxwo/1234?action=CHANGESTATUS&lt;br/&gt;Body: {&quot;newstatus&quot;: &quot;COMP&quot;, &quot;memo&quot;: &quot;Done&quot;, &quot;laborhours&quot;: 3.5}\n    REST-&gt;&gt;Java: Route request to ScriptActionHandler\n    Java-&gt;&gt;Java: 1. Load MBO (WO 1234)&lt;br/&gt;2. Decode body into &#x27;requestBody&#x27;&lt;br/&gt;3. Inject variables (mbo, request, service)\n    Java-&gt;&gt;Script: Execute OSACTION.MXWO.CHANGESTATUS\n    Script-&gt;&gt;Script: 1. mbo.changeStatus(&quot;COMP&quot;, ...)&lt;br/&gt;2. Add child record in LABTRANS&lt;br/&gt;3. Set responseBody JSON\n    Script-&gt;&gt;Java: Return responseBody\n    Java-&gt;&gt;DB: mbo.getThisMboSet().save() (Automatic Commit)\n    Java-&gt;&gt;Client: HTTP 200 OK + JSON Response</pre></div></p>\n<h4>3. Maximo UI Setup Steps (Step-by-Step):</h4>\n<p>##### Step A: Object Structures App Me Action Register Karein:\n<ol>\n<li>Go to <strong>Object Structures</strong> application (search <code>MXWO</code>).</li>\n<li>Click <strong>More Actions (Select Action)</strong> $\\rightarrow$ <strong>Add/Modify OSLC Actions</strong>.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>New Row</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Action Name</strong>: <code>CHANGESTATUS</code></li>\n<li><strong>Description</strong>: <code>Custom Status Change and Labor Log Action</code></li>\n<li><strong>Script Name</strong>: <code>OSACTION.MXWO.CHANGESTATUS</code> (FldOslcActionScriptName.java enforces the mandatory <code>OSACTION.<OSNAME>.<ACTIONNAME></code> format).</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li>Click <strong>OK</strong> & Save.</li></p>\n<p></ol>\n##### Step B: Automation Scripts App Me Script Create Karein:\n<ol>\n<li>Go to <strong>Automation Scripts</strong> application.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Create</strong> $\\rightarrow$ <strong>Script for Integration</strong>.</li>\n<li>Select:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Integration Direction</strong>: <code>OSACTION</code></li>\n<li><strong>Object Structure</strong>: <code>MXWO</code></li>\n<li><strong>Action Name</strong>: <code>CHANGESTATUS</code></li>\n<li><strong>Script Name</strong>: Automatically generates <code>OSACTION.MXWO.CHANGESTATUS</code> (AutoScript.java).</li>\n<li><strong>Script Language</strong>: <code>python</code> (Jython).</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li>Paste the logic and click <strong>Save & Activate</strong>.</li></p>\n<p></ol>\n<h4>4. Injected Implicit Variables (Runtime Context):</h4></p>\n<p>ScriptActionHandler.java runtime par script ke andar automatically ye variables inject karta hai:</p>\n<table class=\"ibm-data-table\">\n<thead><tr>\n<th>Variable Name</th>\n<th>Java Data Type</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>mbo</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>psdi.mbo.MboRemote</code></td>\n<td>Target single MBO record (jab resource URL e.g. <code>/os/mxwo/1234?action=...</code> call hota hai).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>mboset</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>psdi.mbo.MboSetRemote</code></td>\n<td>Target MboSet (jab collection-level URL <code>/os/mxwo?action=...</code> call hota hai).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>requestBody</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>java.lang.String</code></td>\n<td>Incoming HTTP request body payload (JSON/XML UTF-8 String).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>responseBody</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>java.lang.Object</code> (Out variable)</td>\n<td>Client ko return karne ke liye custom JSON String, Byte array, ya MBO object.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>service</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>ScriptService</code></td>\n<td>Helper object (JSON parsing, logging, HTTP calls, error throwing).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>request</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>com.ibm.tivoli.maximo.oslc.provider.OslcRequest</code></td>\n<td>Current HTTP request details (headers, query params, URI info).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>responseHeaders</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>java.util.Map<String, String></code></td>\n<td>HTTP response headers (default <code>content-type: application/json</code>).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>userInfo</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>psdi.security.UserInfo</code></td>\n<td>Logged-in Maximo user session info.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>httpMethod</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>java.lang.String</code></td>\n<td>HTTP Method name (<code>POST</code>, <code>PATCH</code>, <code>GET</code>).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>actionName</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>java.lang.String</code></td>\n<td>Triggered Action identifier (e.g. <code>CHANGESTATUS</code>).</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h4>5. Complete Production-Ready Jython Example (<code>OSACTION.MXWO.CHANGESTATUS</code>):</h4>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>Jython (Python)</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre># Script Name: OSACTION.MXWO.CHANGESTATUS\n# Language: Jython (Python)\n# Trigger URL: POST /maximo/oslc/os/mxwo/54321?action=CHANGESTATUS\n# Request Payload:\n# {\n#   &quot;newstatus&quot;: &quot;COMP&quot;,\n#   &quot;memo&quot;: &quot;Motor replacement completed and tested successfully&quot;,\n#   &quot;laborhours&quot;: 3.5\n# }\n<p>import java.util.Date</p>\n<p># 1. Incoming HTTP Request Body ko parse karna\nif requestBody is not None:\n    req_json = service.tojsonobject(requestBody)\n    target_status = req_json.get(&quot;newstatus&quot;)\n    status_memo = req_json.get(&quot;memo&quot;)\n    actual_hours = req_json.get(&quot;laborhours&quot;)\nelse:\n    target_status = None\n    status_memo = &quot;Updated via Integration Action&quot;\n    actual_hours = 0.0</p>\n<p>service.log_info(&quot;Executing OSACTION CHANGESTATUS for WO: &quot; + (mbo.getString(&quot;WONUM&quot;) if mbo is not None else &quot;NONE&quot;))</p>\n<p># 2. Basic Validations\nif mbo is None:\n    service.error(&quot;workorder&quot;, &quot;noworkorderfound&quot;)</p>\n<p>if target_status is None:\n    service.error(&quot;workorder&quot;, &quot;nostatusprovided&quot;)</p>\n<p># 3. Maximo MBO Business Logic Execution\n# (a) Status Change with Java Method\nmbo.changeStatus(target_status, java.util.Date(), status_memo, 11L)</p>\n<p># (b) Optional: Child Record Creation (e.g. Actual Labor Trans)\nif actual_hours is not None and float(actual_hours) &gt; 0:\n    labtrans_set = mbo.getMboSet(&quot;LABTRANS&quot;)\n    new_lab = labtrans_set.add()\n    new_lab.setValue(&quot;LABORCODE&quot;, userInfo.getPersonId(), 11L)\n    new_lab.setValue(&quot;REGULARHRS&quot;, float(actual_hours), 11L)\n    new_lab.setValue(&quot;TRANSDATE&quot;, java.util.Date(), 11L)</p>\n<p># 4. Construct Custom JSON Success Response\nresponse_dict = service.tojsonobject(&quot;{}&quot;)\nresponse_dict.put(&quot;result&quot;, &quot;SUCCESS&quot;)\nresponse_dict.put(&quot;wonum&quot;, mbo.getString(&quot;WONUM&quot;))\nresponse_dict.put(&quot;status&quot;, mbo.getString(&quot;STATUS&quot;))\nresponse_dict.put(&quot;updatedBy&quot;, userInfo.getUserName())\nresponse_dict.put(&quot;message&quot;, &quot;Work order status successfully changed to &quot; + target_status)</p>\n<p># responseBody set karne se client ko exact custom JSON response milega\nresponseBody = service.jsonToString(response_dict)</pre>\n</div></p>\n<h4>6. Important Behind-the-Scenes Behaviors:</h4>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Automatic Database Commit (<code>save()</code>)</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n   Script ke andar aapko <code>mbo.getThisMboSet().save()</code> likhne ki zaroorat <strong>nahi</strong> hoti. ScriptActionHandler.java Line 102 par execution complete hone ke baad Maximo automatically <code>.save()</code> call karta hai.\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Automatic Rollback on Exception</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n   Agar script me koi error aati hai ya aap <code>service.error(...)</code> throw karte hain, toh ScriptActionHandler.java Line 167 database changes ko automatically <strong>rollback</strong> kar deta hai aur client ko <code>HTTP 400 / 500</code> error JSON return karta hai.\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>INTERFACE = 0</code> Execution</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n   <code>OSIN</code> aur <code>OSOUT</code> ki tarah isme alag-alag functions (<code>def beforeMboData()</code>) nahi hote. Script poori top-to-bottom procedural tareeqe se execute hoti hai.\n</section>"
  },
  "mif-channel-exits": {
    "id": "mif-channel-exits",
    "title": "7.6: Channel Exits: User Exits & External Exits",
    "subtitle": "External Exit (erData outer boundary) vs User Exit (irData Maximo business domain).",
    "html": "<h1>7.6: Channel Exits: User Exits & External Exits</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">External Exit (erData outer boundary) vs User Exit (irData Maximo business domain).</p>\n<section>\n<p>Channel exits transform messages in Publish Channels, Enterprise Services, and Invoke Channels. They are executed by ScriptUserExit.java and ScriptExternalExit.java.</p>\n<h3>1. What Problems Do They Solve?</h3>\n<h4>A. External Exit (<code>ScriptExternalExit.java</code>) \u2014 External Format & Protocol Adapter</h4>\n<em> <strong>Problem</strong>: Maximo uses standard XML/JSON schemas (<code><SyncMXWO></code>, <code><WORKORDER></code>), but external systems (SAP, Salesforce, custom partner APIs) require proprietary structures, custom outer envelopes, cryptographic signatures (HMAC-SHA256), Base64 encoding, or specialized date formats.\n</em> <strong>Solution</strong>:\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Inbound (<code>EXTEXIT.IN</code>)</strong>: Receives raw external payloads, decrypts/sanitizes them, and reshapes them into standard MIF structures before processing rules run.</li>\n<li><strong>Outbound (<code>EXTEXIT.OUT</code>)</strong>: Formats outgoing payloads to match external target schemas right before network dispatch (e.g. injecting authentication tokens, timestamps, or wrapper envelopes).</li>\n<p></ul>\n<h4>B. User Exit (<code>ScriptUserExit.java</code>) \u2014 Internal Business Rule & Policy Enforcer</h4>\n<em> <strong>Problem</strong>: Organizations enforce internal Maximo business rules that integration pipelines must obey:\n<ul>\n<li>Conditionally suppressing outbound transactions without generating queue errors (e.g. export only approved high-priority work orders).</li>\n<li>Enriching inbound messages by looking up supplementary data from other Maximo tables (e.g. resolving Supervisor and Cost Center from an incoming Employee ID).</li>\n<li>Rejecting inbound updates that violate Maximo business state (e.g. updates on decommissioned assets).</li>\n</ul>\n</em> <strong>Solution</strong>:\n<ul>\n<li>*<em>Inbound (<code>USEREXIT.IN.</em></code>)<strong>: Validates business rules and performs database lookups before data touches the MBO layer.</li>\n<li></strong>Outbound (<code>USEREXIT.OUT.<em></code>)</em>*: Evaluates business criteria and calls <code>service.raiseSkipTransaction()</code> to silently drop transactions if criteria are not met.</li></p>\n<p></ul>\n<h3>2. Architecture Boundary & Comparison Matrix</h3></p>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>CODE</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre>+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n<table class=\"ibm-data-table\">\n<thead><tr>\n<th>MAXIMO MIF ARCHITECTURE</th>\n</tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>[External Network / Third Party] &lt;---&gt; [ EXTERNAL EXIT ] &lt;---&gt; [ PROCESSING RULES / XSLT ]</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>(erData Scope)</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>v</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>[Maximo Business Domain / MBOs]  &lt;---&gt; [ USER EXIT ]     &lt;---&gt; [ OBJECT STRUCTURE (OSIN/OSOUT) ]</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>(irData Scope)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>\n</div>\n<table class=\"ibm-data-table\">\n<thead><tr>\n<th>Feature / Comparison</th>\n<th>External Exit (<code>ScriptExternalExit.java</code>)</th>\n<th>User Exit (<code>ScriptUserExit.java</code>)</th>\n</tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>System Boundary</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Network / External Boundary</strong>: Sits between Maximo and external systems.</td>\n<td><strong>Maximo Application Domain</strong>: Sits between Channel Rules and Object Structure/MBOs.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Primary Responsibility</strong></td>\n<td>External schema compatibility, wrapper envelopes, payload encryption/decryption, security headers.</td>\n<td>Maximo business rules, cross-field validation, database lookups, conditional filtering (<code>raiseSkipTransaction</code>).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Data Structure Scope</strong></td>\n<td>Operates primarily on <strong><code>erData</code></strong> (External Record Data).</td>\n<td>Operates on <strong><code>irData</code></strong> (Internal Record Data) and <strong><code>erData</code></strong>.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Inbound Execution</strong></td>\n<td><strong>First Stage (<code>EXTEXIT.IN</code>)</strong>: Before processing rules / XSLT.</td>\n<td><strong>Post-Rules (<code>USEREXIT.IN.AFTER</code>)</strong> or <strong>MBO Level (<code>USEREXIT.IN.MBO</code>)</strong>.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Outbound Execution</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Final Stage (<code>EXTEXIT.OUT</code>)</strong>: Immediately prior to End Point dispatch.</td>\n<td><strong>Initial Stage (<code>USEREXIT.OUT.BEFORE</code>)</strong>: Immediately after Object Structure export.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Can Modify MBO Directly?</strong></td>\n<td>\u274c No.</td>\n<td>\u2714\ufe0f Yes (<code>USEREXIT.IN.MBO</code> hook provides direct <code>mbo</code> access).</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h3>3. Execution Pipelines</h3>\n<h4>Inbound Pipeline (Enterprise Service):</h4>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\"><div class=\"ibm-code-header\"><span>Architecture Flowchart / Diagram</span></div><pre class=\"flowchart-pre\">flowchart TD\n    A[Inbound Raw Payload] --&gt; B[&quot;1. External Exit: EXTEXIT.IN&lt;br/&gt;(Clean/Decrypt erData)&quot;]\n    B --&gt; C[&quot;2. User Exit: USEREXIT.IN.BEFORE&lt;br/&gt;(Pre-Rule erData Validations)&quot;]\n    C --&gt; D[&quot;3. Processing Rules / XSLT&lt;br/&gt;(Transform erData to irData)&quot;]\n    D --&gt; E[&quot;4. User Exit: USEREXIT.IN.AFTER&lt;br/&gt;(Enrich irData with DB lookups)&quot;]\n    E --&gt; F[&quot;5. User Exit MBO: USEREXIT.IN.MBO&lt;br/&gt;(Direct MBO property updates)&quot;]\n    F --&gt; G[&quot;6. Object Structure: OSIN.&lt;OSNAME&gt;&lt;br/&gt;(beforeMboData -&gt; afterMboData -&gt; preSaveRules)&quot;]\n    G --&gt; H[(Database Commit)]</pre></div>\n<h4>Outbound Pipeline (Publish Channel):</h4>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\"><div class=\"ibm-code-header\"><span>Architecture Flowchart / Diagram</span></div><pre class=\"flowchart-pre\">flowchart TD\n    A[Maximo MBO Event Trigger] --&gt; B[&quot;1. Object Structure: OSOUT.&lt;OSNAME&gt;&lt;br/&gt;(skipMbo, overrideValues, skipCols)&quot;]\n    B --&gt; C[&quot;2. User Exit: USEREXIT.OUT.BEFORE&lt;br/&gt;(Modify irData, evaluate business skip)&quot;]\n    C --&gt; D[&quot;3. Processing Rules / XSLT&lt;br/&gt;(Transform irData to erData)&quot;]\n    D --&gt; E[&quot;4. User Exit: USEREXIT.OUT.AFTER&lt;br/&gt;(Modify generated erData &amp; irData)&quot;]\n    E --&gt; F[&quot;5. External Exit: EXTEXIT.OUT&lt;br/&gt;(Payload wrappers, security headers)&quot;]\n    F --&gt; G[End Point / Router Handler -&gt; Network Dispatch]</pre></div>\n<h3>4. Production Jython Examples</h3>\n<h4>External Exit Example (<code>PUBLISH.MYWOEXP.EXTEXIT.OUT</code>):</h4>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>Jython (Python)</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre># Script Name: PUBLISH.MYWOEXP.EXTEXIT.OUT\n# Language: Jython (Python)\n<p>import java.util.Date\nimport java.text.SimpleDateFormat</p>\n<p>service.log_info(&quot;--&gt; Executing External Exit OUT for: &quot; + ifaceName)</p>\n<p>if erData is not None:\n    # Inject external vendor-specific headers and timestamp\n    sdf = java.text.SimpleDateFormat(&quot;yyyy-MM-dd&#x27;T&#x27;HH:mm:ssXXX&quot;)\n    erData.setCurrentData(&quot;DISPATCH_TIMESTAMP&quot;, sdf.format(java.util.Date()))\n    erData.setCurrentData(&quot;API_VERSION&quot;, &quot;v2.4&quot;)\n    \n    # Inject secure API digest token\n    api_token = service.getProperty(&quot;mxe.integration.vendor.token&quot;)\n    erData.setCurrentData(&quot;AUTH_TOKEN&quot;, api_token)</pre>\n</div></p>\n<h4>User Exit Example (<code>PUBLISH.MYWOEXP.USEREXIT.OUT.BEFORE</code>):</h4>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>Jython (Python)</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre># Script Name: PUBLISH.MYWOEXP.USEREXIT.OUT.BEFORE\n# Language: Jython (Python)\n<p>service.log_info(&quot;--&gt; Executing User Exit OUT BEFORE for: &quot; + ifaceName)</p>\n<p>status = irData.getCurrentData(&quot;STATUS&quot;)\nworktype = irData.getCurrentData(&quot;WORKTYPE&quot;)</p>\n<p># Business Rule: Conditionally drop unapproved emergency work orders\nif worktype == &quot;EM&quot; and status != &quot;APPR&quot;:\n    service.log_info(&quot;Skipping unapproved emergency work order: &quot; + irData.getCurrentData(&quot;WONUM&quot;))\n    service.raiseSkipTransaction()  # Drops transaction silently without queue error</p>\n<p># Enrich internal record data\nsupervisor = irData.getCurrentData(&quot;SUPERVISOR&quot;)\nif supervisor is not None:\n    irData.setCurrentData(&quot;CUSTOM_DEPT&quot;, &quot;MAINTENANCE_OPS&quot;)</pre>\n</div></p>\n</section>",
    "title_hi": "7.6: Channel Exits: User Exits Aur External Exits",
    "subtitle_hi": "External Exit (erData adapter) aur User Exit (irData business rules) ka complete comparison.",
    "html_hi": "<h1>7.6: Channel Exits: User Exits Aur External Exits</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">External Exit (erData adapter) aur User Exit (irData business rules) ka complete comparison.</p>\n<section>\n<p>Publish Channels, Enterprise Services aur Invoke Channels me message payload transformation ke liye <strong>Exits</strong> use hote hain. Inhe ScriptUserExit.java aur ScriptExternalExit.java execute karte hain.</p>\n<h3>1. External Exit vs User Exit: Ye Dono Kaunsi Problem Solve Karte Hain?</h3>\n<h4>A. External Exit (<code>ScriptExternalExit.java</code>) \u2014 Kya Problem Solve Karta Hai?</h4>\n<em> <strong>Problem</strong>: Maximo ka apna ek fixed XML/JSON format hota hai. Lekin duniya ke doosre systems (SAP, Salesforce, Custom APIs) Maximo ka format nahi samajhte. Unhe specific JSON/XML envelopes, specialized headers (jaise security token, digest hash), ya custom date formats chahiye hote hain.\n</em> <strong>Solution (External Translator)</strong>:\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Inbound (<code>EXTEXIT.IN</code>)</strong>: Bahar se jo bhi ajeeb-o-gareeb non-standard data, encrypted string, ya proprietary wrapper aaya hai, use sabse pehle decrypt, sanitize, aur Maximo ke samajhne layak structure me transform karta hai.</li>\n<li><strong>Outbound (<code>EXTEXIT.OUT</code>)</strong>: Maximo se nikle huye standard data ko network pe bhejne se theek pehle target vendor ke required schema me convert karta hai (e.g. adding authentication headers, HMAC signature, timestamp tags).</li>\n<p></ul>\n<h4>B. User Exit (<code>ScriptUserExit.java</code>) \u2014 Kya Problem Solve Karta Hai?</h4>\n<em> <strong>Problem</strong>: Har organization ke Maximo me apne <strong>Business Domain Rules</strong> hote hain. Integration data ko Maximo database ke data aur business rules ke sath align karna zaroori hota hai:\n<ul>\n<li>Kuch records ko silently drop karna (e.g. low priority work orders export nahi hone chahiye).</li>\n<li>External system se sirf ID aayi hai, lekin Maximo me save karne se pehle doosre tables se data lookup karke enrich karna hai.</li>\n<li>Agar incoming record Maximo business state se match nahi karta (e.g. asset decommissioned hai), toh transaction ko reject karna.</li>\n</ul>\n</em> <strong>Solution (Internal Business Inspector)</strong>:\n<ul>\n<li>*<em>Inbound (<code>USEREXIT.IN.</em></code>)<strong>: Maximo MBO tak data pahunchne se pehle business validations apply karta hai aur database lookup karke missing fields bharta hai.</li>\n<li></strong>Outbound (<code>USEREXIT.OUT.<em></code>)<strong>: Export hone se pehle decide karta hai ki kya record business criteria match karta hai? Agar nahi, toh <code>service.raiseSkipTransaction()</code> se chupchap drop kar deta hai bina koi error throw kiye.</li></p>\n<p></ul>\n<h3>2. Architecture Boundary & Summary Matrix</h3></p>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>CODE</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre>+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n<table class=\"ibm-data-table\">\n<thead><tr>\n<th>MAXIMO MIF ARCHITECTURE</th>\n</tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>[External Network / Third Party] &lt;---&gt; [ EXTERNAL EXIT ] &lt;---&gt; [ PROCESSING RULES / XSLT ]</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>(erData Scope)</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>v</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>[Maximo Business Domain / MBOs]  &lt;---&gt; [ USER EXIT ]     &lt;---&gt; [ OBJECT STRUCTURE (OSIN/OSOUT) ]</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>(irData Scope)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>\n</div>\n<table class=\"ibm-data-table\">\n<thead><tr>\n<th>Feature / Comparison</th>\n<th>External Exit (<code>ScriptExternalExit.java</code>)</th>\n<th>User Exit (<code>ScriptUserExit.java</code>)</th>\n</tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>System Boundary</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Network / External Boundary</strong>: Maximo aur Bahar ki duniya ke beech baithta hai.</td>\n<td><strong>Maximo Application Domain</strong>: Channel Rules aur Object Structure ke beech baithta hai.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Kaunsi Problem Solve Karta Hai?</strong></td>\n<td>Third-party protocols, proprietary JSON/XML schemas, payload encryption/decryption, custom wrapper tags, external header adjustments.</td>\n<td>Maximo business rules, cross-field validation, DB lookups, business filtering (<code>raiseSkipTransaction</code>), internal data enrichment.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Data Structure</strong></td>\n<td>Primarily operates on <strong><code>erData</code></strong> (External Record Data).</td>\n<td>Operates on <strong><code>irData</code></strong> (Internal Record Data) and <strong><code>erData</code></strong>.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Execution Point (Inbound)</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Sabse Pehle (<code>EXTEXIT.IN</code>)</strong>: Incoming raw external message ko parse/clean karne ke liye.</td>\n<td><strong>Rules Ke Baad (<code>USEREXIT.IN.AFTER</code>)</strong> ya <strong>MBO Level (<code>USEREXIT.IN.MBO</code>)</strong>.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Execution Point (Outbound)</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Sabse Aakhiri (<code>EXTEXIT.OUT</code>)</strong>: End Point par raw bytes dispatch hone se theek pehle.</td>\n<td><strong>Sabse Pehle (<code>USEREXIT.OUT.BEFORE</code>)</strong>: Object Structure se data nikalne ke theek baad.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Can Modify MBO Directly?</strong></td>\n<td>\u274c Nahi.</td>\n<td>\u2714\ufe0f Haan (<code>USEREXIT.IN.MBO</code> hook ke through).</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h3>2. <code>irData</code> vs <code>erData</code> Ka Deep Concept</h3>\n<ul>\n<li></strong><code>irData</code> (Internal Record Data)<strong>:</li>\n<li>Yeh Maximo ke internal Object Structure hierarchy format me hota hai (e.g. <code>MXWO -> WORKORDER -> LABTRANS</code>).</li>\n<li>Iske XML tags Maximo database column names se match karte hain (e.g. <code><WONUM></code>, <code><STATUS></code>, <code><SITEID></code>).</li>\n<li></strong><code>erData</code> (External Record Data)</em><em>:</li>\n<li>Yeh external target system ke format me hota hai (e.g. SAP Idoc, Salesforce JSON, Oracle EBS XML).</li>\n<li>Isme external field names hote hain (e.g. <code><Order_Id></code>, <code><External_State></code>).</li>\n<p></ul>\n<h3>3. Detailed Execution Flow Diagrams</h3></p>\n<h4>Inbound Pipeline (Enterprise Service - Data Entering Maximo):</h4>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\"><div class=\"ibm-code-header\"><span>Architecture Flowchart / Diagram</span></div><pre class=\"flowchart-pre\">flowchart TD\n    A[Incoming Raw Payload] --&gt; B[&quot;1. External Exit: EXTEXIT.IN&lt;br/&gt;(Clean/Decrypt erData)&quot;]\n    B --&gt; C[&quot;2. User Exit: USEREXIT.IN.BEFORE&lt;br/&gt;(Pre-Rule erData Validations)&quot;]\n    C --&gt; D[&quot;3. Processing Rules / XSLT&lt;br/&gt;(Transform erData to irData)&quot;]\n    D --&gt; E[&quot;4. User Exit: USEREXIT.IN.AFTER&lt;br/&gt;(Enrich irData with Maximo DB lookups)&quot;]\n    E --&gt; F[&quot;5. User Exit MBO: USEREXIT.IN.MBO&lt;br/&gt;(Direct MBO property/field updates)&quot;]\n    F --&gt; G[&quot;6. Object Structure: OSIN.&lt;OSNAME&gt;&lt;br/&gt;(beforeMboData -&gt; afterMboData -&gt; preSaveRules)&quot;]\n    G --&gt; H[(Maximo Database Commit)]</pre></div>\n<h4>Outbound Pipeline (Publish Channel - Data Leaving Maximo):</h4>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\"><div class=\"ibm-code-header\"><span>Architecture Flowchart / Diagram</span></div><pre class=\"flowchart-pre\">flowchart TD\n    A[Maximo MBO Event Trigger] --&gt; B[&quot;1. Object Structure: OSOUT.&lt;OSNAME&gt;&lt;br/&gt;(skipMbo, overrideValues, skipCols)&quot;]\n    B --&gt; C[&quot;2. User Exit: USEREXIT.OUT.BEFORE&lt;br/&gt;(Modify irData, evaluate business skip)&quot;]\n    C --&gt; D[&quot;3. Processing Rules / XSLT&lt;br/&gt;(Transform irData to erData)&quot;]\n    D --&gt; E[&quot;4. User Exit: USEREXIT.OUT.AFTER&lt;br/&gt;(Modify generated erData &amp; irData)&quot;]\n    E --&gt; F[&quot;5. External Exit: EXTEXIT.OUT&lt;br/&gt;(Final payload wrapper, formatting, encryption)&quot;]\n    F --&gt; G[End Point / Router Handler -&gt; Network Dispatch]</pre></div>\n<h3>4. Implicit Variables in Exits</h3>\n<p>Exits top-to-bottom run hoti hain (koi specific <code>def function()</code> likhne ki zaroorat nahi hoti). Runtime par ye implicit variables available hote hain:</p>\n<table class=\"ibm-data-table\">\n<thead><tr>\n<th>Variable</th>\n<th>Java Type</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>irData</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>psdi.iface.mic.StructureData</code></td>\n<td>Internal record data structure (Maximo schema).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>erData</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>psdi.iface.mic.StructureData</code></td>\n<td>External record data structure (External schema).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>ifaceName</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>java.lang.String</code></td>\n<td>Channel ya Service ka naam (e.g. <code>MYWOEXP</code>).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>ifaceType</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>java.lang.String</code></td>\n<td><code>PUBLISHCHANNEL</code>, <code>ENTERPRISESERVICE</code>, ya <code>INVOKECHANNEL</code>.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>messageType</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>java.lang.String</code></td>\n<td><code>Sync</code>, <code>Create</code>, <code>Update</code>, <code>Query</code>, etc.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>extSystem</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>java.lang.String</code></td>\n<td>External system name (e.g. <code>EXTSYS1</code>).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>osName</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>java.lang.String</code></td>\n<td>Object structure identifier.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>userInfo</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>psdi.security.UserInfo</code></td>\n<td>Session user details.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>conn</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>java.sql.Connection</code></td>\n<td>Active JDBC database connection.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>service</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>ScriptService</code></td>\n<td>Helper object for logging, skip transactions, HTTP calls.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h3>5. Production Jython Examples</h3>\n<h4>Example A: External Exit Script (<code>PUBLISH.MYWOEXP.EXTEXIT.OUT</code>)</h4>\n</em>Scenario: Outbound XML me third-party vendor ka authentication signature aur timestamp header wrap karna.<em>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>Jython (Python)</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre># Script Name: PUBLISH.MYWOEXP.EXTEXIT.OUT\n# Language: Jython\n<p>import java.util.Date\nimport java.text.SimpleDateFormat</p>\n<p>service.log_info(&quot;--&gt; Executing External Exit OUT for: &quot; + ifaceName)</p>\n<p>if erData is not None:\n    # Target system specific header tags inject karna\n    sdf = java.text.SimpleDateFormat(&quot;yyyy-MM-dd&#x27;T&#x27;HH:mm:ssXXX&quot;)\n    current_timestamp = sdf.format(java.util.Date())\n    \n    erData.setCurrentData(&quot;EXTERNAL_DISPATCH_TS&quot;, current_timestamp)\n    erData.setCurrentData(&quot;INTEGRATION_VERSION&quot;, &quot;v2.4&quot;)\n    \n    # Custom vendor security token inject karna\n    api_token = service.getProperty(&quot;mxe.integration.vendor.token&quot;)\n    erData.setCurrentData(&quot;AUTH_DIGEST&quot;, api_token)</pre>\n</div></p>\n<h4>Example B: User Exit Script (<code>PUBLISH.MYWOEXP.USEREXIT.OUT.BEFORE</code>)</h4>\n</em>Scenario: Business validation check karke certain transactions ko silently skip karna ya internal fields enrich karna.*\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>Jython (Python)</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre># Script Name: PUBLISH.MYWOEXP.USEREXIT.OUT.BEFORE\n# Language: Jython\n<p>service.log_info(&quot;--&gt; Executing User Exit OUT BEFORE for: &quot; + ifaceName)</p>\n<p># irData se internal Maximo values read karna\nstatus = irData.getCurrentData(&quot;STATUS&quot;)\nworktype = irData.getCurrentData(&quot;WORKTYPE&quot;)</p>\n<p># Business Rule: Agar internal emergency ticket nahi hai toh export mat karo\nif worktype == &quot;EM&quot; and status != &quot;APPR&quot;:\n    service.log_info(&quot;Skipping unapproved emergency work order: &quot; + irData.getCurrentData(&quot;WONUM&quot;))\n    service.raiseSkipTransaction()  # Silently drops transaction without queue error</p>\n<p># Maximo Database se additional data lookup karke irData me inject karna\nsupervisor = irData.getCurrentData(&quot;SUPERVISOR&quot;)\nif supervisor is not None:\n    # Set custom internal field\n    irData.setCurrentData(&quot;CUSTOM_DEPT&quot;, &quot;MAINTENANCE_OPS&quot;)</pre>\n</div></p>\n</section>"
  },
  "mif-event-filters": {
    "id": "mif-event-filters",
    "title": "7.7: Publish Channel Event Filter Scripts",
    "subtitle": "Queueing criteria with evalresult boolean in MaximoEventFilter.java.",
    "html": "<h1>7.7: Publish Channel Event Filter Scripts</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">Queueing criteria with evalresult boolean in MaximoEventFilter.java.</p>\n<section>\n<p>When an MBO is created, updated, or deleted, the Publish Channel event listener fires. Before queueing the message, MaximoEventFilter.java executes an event filter script.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Script Name</strong>: <code>PUBLISH.<CHANNEL_NAME>.EVENTFILTER</code></li>\n<li><strong>Injected Variables</strong>: <code>mbo</code>, <code>ifaceName</code>, <code>osName</code>, <code>userInfo</code>, <code>interactive</code>, <code>service</code></li>\n<li><strong>Return Contract</strong>: The script must set <code>evalresult = True</code> (queue message) or <code>evalresult = False</code> (silently discard).</li>\n<p></ul>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>Jython (Python)</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre># Script Name: PUBLISH.MYWOEXP.EVENTFILTER\n# Target: Export only Approved, High-Priority Work Orders</p>\n<p>status = mbo.getString(&quot;STATUS&quot;)\npriority = mbo.getInt(&quot;WOPRIORITY&quot;)</p>\n<p>if status == &quot;APPR&quot; and priority &lt;= 2:\n    evalresult = True   # Message proceeds to JMS Queue\nelse:\n    evalresult = False  # Message silently discarded</pre>\n</div></p>\n</section>",
    "title_hi": "7.7: Publish Channel Event Filter Scripts",
    "subtitle_hi": "evalresult = True / False se messages ko JMS queue me jane se pehle filter karna.",
    "html_hi": "<h1>7.7: Publish Channel Event Filter Scripts</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">evalresult = True / False se messages ko JMS queue me jane se pehle filter karna.</p>\n<section>\n<p>Jab Maximo me koi MBO create, update, ya delete hota hai, toh Publish Channel listener trigger hota hai. Queue me message daalne se pehle MaximoEventFilter.java event filter script run karta hai.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Script Name</strong>: <code>PUBLISH.<CHANNEL_NAME>.EVENTFILTER</code></li>\n<li><strong>Injected Variables</strong>: <code>mbo</code>, <code>ifaceName</code>, <code>osName</code>, <code>userInfo</code>, <code>interactive</code>, <code>service</code></li>\n<li><strong>Output Return</strong>: Script ke andar <code>evalresult = True</code> ya <code>evalresult = False</code> set karna hota hai.</li>\n<p></ul>\n<h3>Jython Example (<code>PUBLISH.MYWOEXP.EVENTFILTER</code>):</h3></p>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>Jython (Python)</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre># Script Name: PUBLISH.MYWOEXP.EVENTFILTER\n# Target: Sirf Approved aur high priority Work Orders ko hi export karna\n<p>status = mbo.getString(&quot;STATUS&quot;)\npriority = mbo.getInt(&quot;WOPRIORITY&quot;)</p>\n<p># Condition check\nif status == &quot;APPR&quot; and priority &lt;= 2:\n    evalresult = True   # Message Queue me jayega\nelse:\n    evalresult = False  # Message silently discard ho jayega (Queue me nahi jayega)</pre>\n</div></p>\n</section>"
  },
  "mif-endpoint-router": {
    "id": "mif-endpoint-router",
    "title": "7.8: End Point & Router Handler Scripts (SCRIPT Handler)",
    "subtitle": "Custom REST/SOAP dispatching without launch points using ScriptRouterHandler.java.",
    "html": "<h1>7.8: End Point & Router Handler Scripts (SCRIPT Handler)</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">Custom REST/SOAP dispatching without launch points using ScriptRouterHandler.java.</p>\n<section>\n<h3>Why Is There No Launch Point for End Points?</h3>\n<p>In the Automation Scripts application, Launch Points exist for Objects, Attributes, Actions, and Integration Channels, but <strong>there is no Launch Point for End Points</strong>.</p>\n<h4>Architectural Reason:</h4>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>End Points are Handlers, Not Event Listeners</strong>: In MIF, an End Point is a transport/router mechanism (like <code>HTTP</code>, <code>JMS</code>, <code>FLATFILE</code>, <code>WEBSERVICE</code>).</li>\n<li><strong><code>ScriptRouterHandler.java</code> Architecture</strong>: Maximo provides a built-in handler ScriptRouterHandler.java which dynamically invokes a <strong>Standalone Script (Script WITHOUT Launch Point)</strong> specified in the End Point's properties.</li>\n<p></ol>\n<h3>Step-by-Step Configuration Guide</h3></p>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>CODE</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre>Step 1: Create Standalone Script (No Launch Point)\n   [Automation Scripts App] -&gt; Click &quot;Create Script&quot; -&gt; Enter Name: &quot;MY_REST_DISPATCHER&quot;\n                                     |\n                                     v\nStep 2: Create End Point with SCRIPT Handler\n   [End Points App] -&gt; New End Point: &quot;REST_EP&quot; -&gt; Select Handler: &quot;SCRIPT&quot;\n                                     |\n                                     v\nStep 3: Link Script in Properties Table\n   [End Point Properties Table] -&gt; Property &quot;SCRIPT&quot; Value = &quot;MY_REST_DISPATCHER&quot;\n                                     |\n                                     v\nStep 4: Attach End Point to Publish Channel / External System\n   [Publish Channels App] -&gt; End Point = &quot;REST_EP&quot;</pre>\n</div>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Step 1: Create Standalone Script</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Open <strong>Automation Scripts</strong> application.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Create</strong> $\\rightarrow$ <strong>Script</strong> (<em>Script WITHOUT Launch Point</em>).</li>\n<li><strong>Script Name</strong>: <code>MY_REST_DISPATCHER</code>, <strong>Language</strong>: <code>python</code> (Jython).</li>\n<li>Save and set Status to <strong>ACTIVE</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Step 2: Configure End Point</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Open <strong>Integration</strong> $\\rightarrow$ <strong>End Points</strong> application.</li>\n<li>Create New End Point: <code>REST_EP</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Handler</strong>: Select <strong><code>SCRIPT</code></strong>.</li>\n<li>In the <strong>End Point Properties</strong> table, find the auto-generated <strong><code>SCRIPT</code></strong> property and set its <strong>Value</strong> to <code>MY_REST_DISPATCHER</code>.</li>\n<li>(Optional) Add custom properties (e.g. <code>URL</code>, <code>AUTH_TOKEN</code>, <code>TIMEOUT</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Step 3: Link to Publish Channel</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>In <strong>Publish Channels</strong> application, set <code>End Point = REST_EP</code>.</li>\n<p></ul>\n<h3>Internal Java Mechanics (ScriptRouterHandler.java)</h3></p>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>Java (Maximo Core)</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre>// 1. Read target script name from End Point properties\nString scriptName = getPropertyValue(&quot;SCRIPT&quot;);\n<p>// 2. Load compiled script from cache\nScriptInfo scriptInfo = ScriptCache.getInstance().getScriptInfo(scriptName.toUpperCase());</p>\n<p>// 3. Inject variables into script context\nMap&lt;String, Object&gt; context = new HashMap&lt;&gt;();\ncontext.put(&quot;requestData&quot;, data);                            // byte[] raw data\ncontext.put(&quot;requestDataS&quot;, new String(data, &quot;utf-8&quot;));       // UTF-8 String payload\nfor (String key : metaData.keySet()) {\n    context.put(key, metaData.get(key));                     // EndPoint properties (URL, etc.)\n}</p>\n<p>// 4. Execute script\nScriptDriverFactory.getInstance().getScriptDriver(scriptName).runScript(scriptName, context);</p>\n<p>// 5. Return response data to caller\nObject respData = context.get(&quot;responseData&quot;);\nreturn (respData instanceof String) ? ((String)respData).getBytes(&quot;utf-8&quot;) : (byte[])respData;</pre>\n</div></p>\n<h3>Injected Variables:</h3>\n<table class=\"ibm-data-table\">\n<thead><tr>\n<th>Variable</th>\n<th>Type</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>requestData</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>byte[]</code></td>\n<td>Raw outgoing message byte array.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>requestDataS</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>java.lang.String</code></td>\n<td>Outgoing message as UTF-8 string (JSON/XML).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>context</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>java.util.Map</code></td>\n<td>Map containing all configured End Point properties (<code>URL</code>, <code>SCRIPT</code>, etc.).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>responseData</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>String</code> / <code>byte[]</code> <em>(Out)</em></td>\n<td><strong>Return Variable</strong>: Set response received from external service.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>service</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>ScriptService</code></td>\n<td>Helper object for HTTP calls and logging.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h3>Production Jython Example (<code>MY_REST_DISPATCHER</code>):</h3>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>Jython (Python)</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre># Script Name: MY_REST_DISPATCHER\n# Script Type: Standalone Script (Configured in End Point with SCRIPT Handler)\n# Language: Jython (Python)\n<p>service.log_info(&quot;--&gt; Starting End Point SCRIPT Handler Dispatch&quot;)</p>\n<p>target_url = context.get(&quot;URL&quot;)\nauth_token = context.get(&quot;AUTH_TOKEN&quot;)\npayload_string = requestDataS</p>\n<p>if target_url is None:\n    target_url = &quot;https://api.external.com/v1/workorders&quot;</p>\n<p>service.log_info(&quot;Dispatching to URL: &quot; + str(target_url))</p>\n<p>headers = &quot;Content-Type: application/json\\nAccept: application/json&quot;\nif auth_token is not None:\n    headers += &quot;\\nAuthorization: Bearer &quot; + str(auth_token)</p>\n<p>try:\n    json_payload = service.tojsonobject(payload_string)\n    response_json = service.httppostasjson(str(target_url), None, None, headers, json_payload)\n    \n    if response_json is not None:\n        responseData = service.jsonToString(response_json)\n        service.log_info(&quot;External response received: &quot; + str(responseData))\n    else:\n        responseData = &#x27;{&quot;status&quot;:&quot;SUCCESS&quot;, &quot;code&quot;: 200}&#x27;\n        \nexcept Exception as e:\n    service.log_error(&quot;Failed to dispatch REST payload: &quot; + str(e))\n    service.error(&quot;iface&quot;, &quot;endpoint_call_failed&quot;, [str(e)])</pre>\n</div></p>\n</section>",
    "title_hi": "7.8: Endpoint / Router Handler Scripts (SCRIPT Handler)",
    "subtitle_hi": "Bina launch point ke standalone script banakar End Point se custom HTTP/REST API call karna.",
    "html_hi": "<h1>7.8: Endpoint / Router Handler Scripts (SCRIPT Handler)</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">Bina launch point ke standalone script banakar End Point se custom HTTP/REST API call karna.</p>\n<section>\n<h3>End Point Ke Liye Launch Point Kyun Nahi Milta? (Crucial Concept)</h3>\n<p>Jab aap <strong>Automation Scripts</strong> application me jaate hain, toh Launch Point list me Object Structure, Publish Channel, Enterprise Service milte hain lekin <strong>End Point ka koi Launch Point nahi hota</strong>.</p>\n<h4>Iska Reason Kya Hai?</h4>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>End Point is a Handler, Not an Event Listener</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>MIF me End Point koi trigger event nahi hota; yeh ek <strong>Transport / Router Handler</strong> hota hai (jaise <code>HTTP</code>, <code>JMS</code>, <code>FLATFILE</code>, <code>WEBSERVICE</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>ScriptRouterHandler.java</code> Architecture</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Maximo built-in ScriptRouterHandler.java provide karta hai.</li>\n<li>Yeh handler ek <strong>Standalone Script</strong> (Script WITHOUT Launch Point) ko End Point ki property ke zariye call karta hai.</li>\n<p></ul>\n<h3>Step-by-Step UI Setup Guide</h3></p>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>CODE</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre>Step 1: Create Standalone Script (No Launch Point)\n   [Automation Scripts App] -&gt; Click &quot;Create Script&quot; -&gt; Enter Name: &quot;MY_REST_DISPATCHER&quot;\n                                     |\n                                     v\nStep 2: Create End Point with SCRIPT Handler\n   [End Points App] -&gt; New End Point: &quot;REST_EP&quot; -&gt; Select Handler: &quot;SCRIPT&quot;\n                                     |\n                                     v\nStep 3: Link Script in Properties Table\n   [End Point Properties Table] -&gt; Property &quot;SCRIPT&quot; Value = &quot;MY_REST_DISPATCHER&quot;\n                                     |\n                                     v\nStep 4: Attach End Point to Publish Channel / External System\n   [Publish Channels App] -&gt; End Point = &quot;REST_EP&quot;</pre>\n</div>\n<h4>Step 1: Standalone Script Banayein:</h4>\n<ol>\n<li>Go to <strong>Automation Scripts</strong> application.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Create</strong> $\\rightarrow$ <strong>Script</strong> (Option: <em>Create Script</em> bina kisi launch point ke).</li>\n<li><strong>Script Name</strong>: e.g. <code>MY_REST_DISPATCHER</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Script Language</strong>: <code>python</code> (Jython).</li>\n<li>Code likhein aur status ko <strong>ACTIVE</strong> karein.</li>\n<p></ol>\n<h4>Step 2: End Point Configure Karein:</h4>\n<ol>\n<li>Go to <strong>Integration</strong> $\\rightarrow$ <strong>End Points</strong> application.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>New End Point</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>End Point</strong>: <code>REST_EP</code></li>\n<li><strong>Description</strong>: <code>Custom Third-Party REST API Endpoint</code></li>\n<li><strong>Handler</strong>: Select <strong><code>SCRIPT</code></strong> (Dropdown se <code>SCRIPT</code> chunein).</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li>Niche <strong>End Point Properties</strong> table me dekhein:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Maximo automatically <strong><code>SCRIPT</code></strong> property dikhayega.</li>\n<li><code>SCRIPT</code> property ki <strong>Value</strong> me apna script name daalein: <code>MY_REST_DISPATCHER</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li>(Optional) Custom properties add karein (jaise <code>URL</code>, <code>AUTH_KEY</code>, <code>TIMEOUT</code>) jo script me <code>context.get(\"URL\")</code> se read ki ja sakein.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Save</strong>.</li></p>\n<p></ol>\n<h3>Backend Java Execution Mechanics (<code>ScriptRouterHandler.java</code>)</h3></p>\n<p>Jab Publish Channel ya Invoke Channel is End Point par message bhejta hai, toh ScriptRouterHandler.java Line 63-103 execute hota hai:</p>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>Java (Maximo Core)</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre>// 1. End Point Properties se script ka naam read karta hai\nString scriptName = getPropertyValue(&quot;SCRIPT&quot;);\n<p>// 2. ScriptCache se script fetch karta hai\nScriptInfo scriptInfo = ScriptCache.getInstance().getScriptInfo(scriptName.toUpperCase());</p>\n<p>// 3. Context Map me variables inject karta hai\nMap&lt;String, Object&gt; context = new HashMap&lt;&gt;();\ncontext.put(&quot;requestData&quot;, data);                            // byte[] raw data\ncontext.put(&quot;requestDataS&quot;, new String(data, &quot;utf-8&quot;));       // UTF-8 String payload\n// Saari EndPoint properties context me daal deta hai\nfor (String key : metaData.keySet()) {\n    context.put(key, metaData.get(key));\n}</p>\n<p>// 4. Script execute karta hai\nScriptDriverFactory.getInstance().getScriptDriver(scriptName).runScript(scriptName, context);</p>\n<p>// 5. Script ka return responseData read karke return karta hai\nObject respData = context.get(&quot;responseData&quot;);\nreturn (respData instanceof String) ? ((String)respData).getBytes(&quot;utf-8&quot;) : (byte[])respData;</pre>\n</div></p>\n<h3>Injected Variables in End Point Script:</h3>\n<table class=\"ibm-data-table\">\n<thead><tr>\n<th>Variable</th>\n<th>Type</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>requestData</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>byte[]</code></td>\n<td>Raw outgoing message byte array.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>requestDataS</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>java.lang.String</code></td>\n<td>Outgoing message UTF-8 String format me (JSON/XML).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>context</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>java.util.Map</code></td>\n<td>End Point ki saari configured properties (e.g. <code>URL</code>, <code>SCRIPT</code>, etc.).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>responseData</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>String</code> / <code>byte[]</code> <em>(Out)</em></td>\n<td><strong>Return Variable</strong>: External system se aaya response isme set karein.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>service</code></strong></td>\n<td><code>ScriptService</code></td>\n<td>Helper object for logging, HTTP calls, error throwing.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h3>Complete Production Jython Example (<code>MY_REST_DISPATCHER</code>):</h3>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>Jython (Python)</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre># Script Name: MY_REST_DISPATCHER\n# Script Type: Standalone Script (Configured in End Point with SCRIPT Handler)\n# Language: Jython\n<p>import java.util.HashMap</p>\n<p>service.log_info(&quot;--&gt; Starting End Point Dispatcher Script&quot;)</p>\n<p># 1. End Point Properties read karna\ntarget_url = context.get(&quot;URL&quot;)\nauth_token = context.get(&quot;AUTH_TOKEN&quot;)\npayload_string = requestDataS</p>\n<p>if target_url is None:\n    target_url = &quot;https://api.thirdparty.com/v1/workorders&quot;</p>\n<p>service.log_info(&quot;Dispatching payload to URL: &quot; + str(target_url))</p>\n<p># 2. HTTP Headers prepare karna\nheaders = &quot;Content-Type: application/json\\nAccept: application/json&quot;\nif auth_token is not None:\n    headers += &quot;\\nAuthorization: Bearer &quot; + str(auth_token)</p>\n<p># 3. Payload ko JSON format me convert karke HTTP POST karna\ntry:\n    json_payload = service.tojsonobject(payload_string)\n    \n    # ScriptService ke built-in HTTP POST method se call karna\n    response_json = service.httppostasjson(str(target_url), None, None, headers, json_payload)\n    \n    # 4. Response wapas Maximo router ko pass karna\n    if response_json is not None:\n        responseData = service.jsonToString(response_json)\n        service.log_info(&quot;Successfully received external response: &quot; + str(responseData))\n    else:\n        responseData = &#x27;{&quot;status&quot;:&quot;SUCCESS&quot;, &quot;code&quot;: 200}&#x27;\n        \nexcept Exception as e:\n    service.log_error(&quot;Error dispatching REST payload: &quot; + str(e))\n    # Error throw karne se MIF queue me message retry/error status me chala jayega\n    service.error(&quot;iface&quot;, &quot;endpoint_call_failed&quot;, [str(e)])</pre>\n</div></p>\n</section>"
  },
  "mif-service-api": {
    "id": "mif-service-api",
    "title": "7.9: service Helper Object (ScriptService API Reference)",
    "subtitle": "Built-in methods for HTTP calls, transaction control, logging, and workflow triggers.",
    "html": "<h1>7.9: service Helper Object (ScriptService API Reference)</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">Built-in methods for HTTP calls, transaction control, logging, and workflow triggers.</p>\n<section>\n<p>Every script has an implicit <code>service</code> variable referencing ScriptService.java:</p>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\"><div class=\"ibm-code-header\"><span>Architecture Flowchart / Diagram</span></div><pre class=\"flowchart-pre\">classDiagram\n    class ScriptService {\n        +raiseSkipTransaction()\n        +log_info(msg)\n        +log_debug(msg)\n        +log_error(msg)\n        +httpget(url)\n        +httppost(url, data)\n        +httpgetasjson(url, user, headers, pass)\n        +httppostasjson(url, user, pass, headers, json)\n        +invokeEndpoint(epName, meta, data)\n        +invokeChannel(channelName)\n        +invokeWorkflow(wfName)\n        +invokeScript(scriptName, function, args)\n        +getMboSet(setName, userInfo)\n        +getProperty(propName)\n        +error(group, key, params)\n    }</pre></div>\n<h3>Method Categories:</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Transaction Control</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li><code>service.raiseSkipTransaction()</code>: Drops transaction cleanly without logging queue errors.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Logging</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li><code>service.log_info(\"msg\")</code>, <code>service.log_debug(\"msg\")</code>, <code>service.log_error(\"msg\")</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>HTTP / REST Calls</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li><code>service.httpget(url)</code></li>\n<li><code>service.httppost(url, bodyString)</code></li>\n<li><code>service.httppostasjson(url, user, pass, headers, jsonObject)</code></li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Channel & Workflow Triggers</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li><code>service.invokeChannel(\"CHANNEL_NAME\")</code>: Synchronous Invoke Channel execution.</li>\n<li><code>service.invokeWorkflow(\"WORKFLOW_NAME\")</code>: Triggers Maximo Workflow.</li>\n<li><code>service.invokeEndpoint(\"ENDPOINT_NAME\", metaDataMap, dataString)</code>: Routes data through another End Point.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Database & System Properties</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li><code>service.getMboSet(\"ASSET\", userInfo)</code>: Fetches arbitrary MboSet.</li>\n<li><code>service.getProperty(\"mxe.myproperty\")</code>: Reads system property from <code>MAXPROPVALUE</code>.</li>\n<p></ul></p>\n</section>",
    "title_hi": "7.9: service Helper Object (ScriptService API Reference)",
    "subtitle_hi": "raiseSkipTransaction, httppostasjson, invokeWorkflow, aur logging API methods.",
    "html_hi": "<h1>7.9: service Helper Object (ScriptService API Reference)</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">raiseSkipTransaction, httppostasjson, invokeWorkflow, aur logging API methods.</p>\n<section>\n<p>Har script ke andar <code>service</code> variable (ScriptService.java) automatically inject hota hai. Iske most useful methods:</p>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\"><div class=\"ibm-code-header\"><span>Architecture Flowchart / Diagram</span></div><pre class=\"flowchart-pre\">classDiagram\n    class ScriptService {\n        +raiseSkipTransaction()\n        +log_info(msg)\n        +log_debug(msg)\n        +log_error(msg)\n        +httpget(url)\n        +httppost(url, data)\n        +httpgetasjson(url, user, headers, pass)\n        +httppostasjson(url, user, pass, headers, json)\n        +invokeEndpoint(epName, meta, data)\n        +invokeChannel(channelName)\n        +invokeWorkflow(wfName)\n        +invokeScript(scriptName, function, args)\n        +getMboSet(setName, userInfo)\n        +getProperty(propName)\n        +error(group, key, params)\n    }</pre></div>\n<h3>Main Method Categories:</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Transaction Skip / Drop</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li><code>service.raiseSkipTransaction()</code>: Message ko bina kisi queue error ke quietly skip kar deta hai.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Logging</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li><code>service.log_info(\"message\")</code>: Maximo logging me INFO level log likhta hai.</li>\n<li><code>service.log_debug(\"message\")</code>: DEBUG level log likhta hai.</li>\n<li><code>service.log_error(\"message\")</code>: ERROR level log likhta hai.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>HTTP / REST Calls</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li><code>service.httpget(url)</code>: Simple GET call.</li>\n<li><code>service.httppost(url, bodyString)</code>: Simple POST call.</li>\n<li><code>service.httppostasjson(url, user, pass, headers, jsonArtifact)</code>: Direct JSON POST call.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Channels & Workflows Trigger Karna</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li><code>service.invokeChannel(\"CHANNEL_NAME\")</code>: Synchronous Invoke Channel call.</li>\n<li><code>service.invokeWorkflow(\"WORKFLOW_NAME\")</code>: MBO ke liye Workflow initiate karta hai.</li>\n<li><code>service.invokeEndpoint(\"ENDPOINT_NAME\", metaDataMap, dataString)</code>: Dusra EndPoint trigger karta hai.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Database & Properties</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li><code>service.getMboSet(\"ASSET\", userInfo)</code>: Kisi bhi table ka <code>MboSet</code> fetch karta hai.</li>\n<li><code>service.getProperty(\"mxe.myproperty\")</code>: <code>MAXPROPVALUE</code> se system property read karta hai.</li>\n<p></ul></p>\n</section>"
  },
  "mif-structuredata-api": {
    "id": "mif-structuredata-api",
    "title": "7.10: StructureData XML & JSON Data API Reference",
    "subtitle": "Reading, modifying, and creating child structures in irData, erData, and ctx.getData().",
    "html": "<h1>7.10: StructureData XML & JSON Data API Reference</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">Reading, modifying, and creating child structures in irData, erData, and ctx.getData().</p>\n<section>\n<p>When working with <code>irData</code>, <code>erData</code>, or <code>ctx.getData()</code>, Maximo provides StructureData.java and StructureObject.java:</p>\n<h3>Reading Values:</h3>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>Jython (Python)</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre>siteid = struc.getCurrentData(&quot;SITEID&quot;)\nqty = struc.getCurrentDataAsDouble(&quot;ITEMQTY&quot;)\nreportdate = struc.getCurrentDataAsDate(&quot;REPORTDATE&quot;)\n<p>if not struc.isCurrentDataNull(&quot;ASSETNUM&quot;):\n    asset = struc.getCurrentData(&quot;ASSETNUM&quot;)</pre>\n</div></p>\n<h3>Modifying Values:</h3>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>Jython (Python)</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre>struc.setCurrentData(&quot;STATUS&quot;, &quot;APPR&quot;)\nstruc.setCurrentDataNull(&quot;LEADTIME&quot;)</pre>\n</div>\n<h3>Working with Child Collections:</h3>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>Jython (Python)</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre>labtrans_list = struc.getChildren(&quot;LABTRANS&quot;)\nif labtrans_list is not None:\n    for labtran in labtrans_list:\n        hours = labtran.getCurrentDataAsDouble(&quot;REGULARHRS&quot;)\n<p># Adding a new child structure\nnew_child = struc.createStructureObject(&quot;WOLABS&quot;)\nnew_child.setCurrentData(&quot;CRAFT&quot;, &quot;ELEC&quot;)\nnew_child.setCurrentData(&quot;QUANTITY&quot;, &quot;2&quot;)\nstruc.addChild(new_child)</pre>\n</div></p>\n</section>",
    "title_hi": "7.10: StructureData Se XML/JSON Data Read Aur Modify Karna",
    "subtitle_hi": "getCurrentData, setCurrentData, getChildren, aur createStructureObject ka use.",
    "html_hi": "<h1>7.10: StructureData Se XML/JSON Data Read Aur Modify Karna</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">getCurrentData, setCurrentData, getChildren, aur createStructureObject ka use.</p>\n<section>\n<p>Jab aap <code>irData</code>, <code>erData</code> ya <code>ctx.getData()</code> ke sath kaam karte hain, toh Maximo aapko StructureData.java aur StructureObject.java APIs provide karta hai:</p>\n<h3>Data Read Karne Ke Methods:</h3>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>Jython (Python)</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre># 1. String value lena\nsiteid = struc.getCurrentData(&quot;SITEID&quot;)\n<p># 2. Number / Date lena\nquantity = struc.getCurrentDataAsDouble(&quot;ITEMQTY&quot;)\nreportdate = struc.getCurrentDataAsDate(&quot;REPORTDATE&quot;)</p>\n<p># 3. Check karna ki field null hai ya nahi\nif not struc.isCurrentDataNull(&quot;ASSETNUM&quot;):\n    asset = struc.getCurrentData(&quot;ASSETNUM&quot;)</pre>\n</div></p>\n<h3>Data Write / Modify Karne Ke Methods:</h3>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>Jython (Python)</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre># Value set karna\nstruc.setCurrentData(&quot;STATUS&quot;, &quot;APPR&quot;)\n<p># Field ko null set karna\nstruc.setCurrentDataNull(&quot;LEADTIME&quot;)</pre>\n</div></p>\n<h3>Hierarchy / Child Objects Ke Sath Kaam Karna:</h3>\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>Jython (Python)</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre># Child objects ki list lena (e.g. Work Order ke LABTRANS)\nlabtrans_list = struc.getChildren(&quot;LABTRANS&quot;)\n<p>if labtrans_list is not None:\n    for labtran in labtrans_list:\n        hours = labtran.getCurrentDataAsDouble(&quot;REGULARHRS&quot;)\n        service.log_info(&quot;Labtrans Hours: &quot; + str(hours))</p>\n<p># Naya Child Object create karke add karna\nnew_wols = struc.createStructureObject(&quot;WOLABS&quot;)\nnew_wols.setCurrentData(&quot;CRAFT&quot;, &quot;ELEC&quot;)\nnew_wols.setCurrentData(&quot;QUANTITY&quot;, &quot;2&quot;)\nstruc.addChild(new_wols)</pre>\n</div></p>\n</section>"
  },
  "mif-error-handling": {
    "id": "mif-error-handling",
    "title": "7.11: Error Handling & Production Best Practices (Pro Tips)",
    "subtitle": "Silent skips, structured business errors, memory management, and performance optimizations.",
    "html": "<h1>7.11: Error Handling & Production Best Practices (Pro Tips)</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">Silent skips, structured business errors, memory management, and performance optimizations.</p>\n<section>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Silent Message Suppression</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>In Exits: <code>service.raiseSkipTransaction()</code></li>\n<li>In Object Structure scripts: <code>ctx.skipTxn()</code></li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Throwing Business Errors</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Use <code>service.error(group, key, params)</code> to fail transactions cleanly with localized messages.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Use Loggers over Print Statements</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Always use <code>service.log_info(...)</code> or <code>service.log_debug(...)</code> to respect Maximo loggers (<code>maximo.script.<SCRIPTNAME></code> and <code>maximo.integration</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Memory Management</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>When creating independent <code>MboSet</code> instances via <code>service.getMboSet(...)</code>, ensure proper cleanup or enable <code>mxe.script.autocleanup = 1</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Avoid Heavy Synchronous Calls in DB Transactions</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Perform slow third-party API calls in asynchronous queues or Invoke Channels rather than inside synchronous DB save hooks.</li>\n<p></ul></p>\n</section>",
    "title_hi": "7.11: Error Handling Aur Best Practices (Pro Tips)",
    "subtitle_hi": "service.error, memory cleanup, logger configuration, aur architecture best practices.",
    "html_hi": "<h1>7.11: Error Handling Aur Best Practices (Pro Tips)</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">service.error, memory cleanup, logger configuration, aur architecture best practices.</p>\n<section>\n<h3>1. Message Ko Silent Drop Karna (<code>SKIP_TRANSACTION</code>):</h3>\nAgar koi message criteria match nahi karta aur aap chahte hain ki woh Message Tracking me error na bane aur queue me retry na ho, toh silently skip karein:\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Exits me</strong>: <code>service.raiseSkipTransaction()</code></li>\n<li><strong>Object Structure me</strong>: <code>ctx.skipTxn()</code></li>\n<p></ul>\n<h3>2. User-Facing Error Throw Karna:</h3>\nAgar transaction ko fail karke queue me error banana hai:\n<div class=\"ibm-code-block\">\n  <div class=\"ibm-code-header\">\n    <span>Jython (Python)</span>\n    <button class=\"btn-copy\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  </div>\n  <pre>service.error(&quot;workorder&quot;, &quot;invalid_status&quot;, [&quot;APPR&quot;])</pre>\n</div></p>\n<h3>3. Print Statements Ki Jagah Logger Use Karein:</h3>\nHamesha <code>service.log_info(...)</code> ya <code>service.log_debug(...)</code> use karein. Yeh logs Maximo Logging app ke <code>maximo.script.<SCRIPTNAME></code> aur <code>maximo.integration</code> loggers se govern hote hain.\n<h3>4. Memory Leaks Se Bachna:</h3>\nAgar aap script ke andar <code>service.getMboSet(...)</code> ya <code>MXServer.getMXServer().getMboSet(...)</code> se naye <code>MboSet</code> banate hain, toh unhe use ke baad cleanup zaroor karein ya Maximo property <code>mxe.script.autocleanup = 1</code> enable rakhein.\n<h3>5. Heavy Synchronous Calls Transaction Me Mat Karein:</h3>\nInbound <code>beforeMboData</code> ya <code>preSaveRules</code> ke andar lambi external third-party HTTP calls karne se database locks badh sakte hain. External heavy integrations ke liye <strong>Asynchronous JMS Queues</strong> ya <strong>Invoke Channels</strong> ka use karein.\n</section>"
  },
  "mif-faq-doubts": {
    "id": "mif-faq-doubts",
    "title": "7.12: Frequently Asked Questions & Deep Technical Doubts",
    "subtitle": "INTERFACE flag differences, Invocable hook resolution, and hardcoded naming lookup keys.",
    "html": "<h1>7.12: Frequently Asked Questions & Deep Technical Doubts</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">INTERFACE flag differences, Invocable hook resolution, and hardcoded naming lookup keys.</p>\n<section>\n<h3>Q1: What is the significance of <code>INTERFACE = 1</code> vs <code>INTERFACE = 0</code> in the <code>AUTOSCRIPT</code> table?</h3>\n<p><strong>Answer:</strong>\nThe <code>INTERFACE</code> flag informs the script driver how to compile and execute the script:\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>INTERFACE = 0</code> (Procedural Script)</strong>: Executed top-to-bottom sequentially as a single unit via <code>cs.eval(sc)</code>. Used for Object, Attribute, Action, <code>OSQUERY</code>, and <code>OSACTION</code> scripts.</li>\n<li><strong><code>INTERFACE = 1</code> (Function Library Callback Script)</strong>: Loaded into <code>invocableScriptCache</code> by ScriptCacheImpl.java. The engine invokes specific lifecycle functions on-demand using <code>((Invocable)engine).invokeFunction(functionName, args)</code>. Used for <code>OSIN</code> and <code>OSOUT</code>.</li></p>\n<p></ul>\n<h3>Q2: How does <code>Invocable</code> know which function exists in the script? What happens to unimplemented hooks?</h3></p>\n<p><strong>Answer:</strong>\nDevelopers are <strong>not required</strong> to implement all 8 lifecycle hooks. You only implement the specific hook needed (e.g. <code>beforeMboData</code>).\n<ul>\n<li>When a lifecycle event fires, the engine queries the script: <code>Object scrFunction = engine.get(functionName);</code>.</li>\n<li>If the function is not defined, <code>scrFunction == null</code> and the engine immediately returns <code>invokeStatus = false</code>.</li>\n<li>MosProcessImpl.java Line 440 detects this and falls back to standard Out-of-the-Box (OOB) Maximo processing.</li></p>\n<p></ul>\n<h3>Q3: Are naming conventions (like <code>OSIN.<OSNAME></code>) strictly mandatory?</h3></p>\n<p><strong>Answer:</strong>\n<strong>Yes, strictly mandatory.</strong>\nMaximo integration classes hardcode the lookup keys when loading scripts from cache:\n<ul>\n<li><code>this.scriptName = \"OSIN.\" + mosName;</code> (MosProcess.java Line 190).</li>\n<li><code>this.scriptName = \"OSOUT.\" + mosName;</code> (MosDefinitionImpl.java Line 186).</li>\n</ul>\nArbitrary names will not be found in cache and will be bypassed.</p>\n<h3>Q4: What is the difference between <code>OSQUERY</code>, <code>OSACTION</code>, and <code>OSIN</code>/<code>OSOUT</code>?</h3>\n<table class=\"ibm-data-table\">\n<thead><tr>\n<th>Dimension</th>\n<th><code>OSIN</code> / <code>OSOUT</code></th>\n<th><code>OSQUERY</code></th>\n<th><code>OSACTION</code></th>\n</tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Primary Goal</strong></td>\n<td>Inbound/Outbound serialization</td>\n<td>Dynamic REST query filtering</td>\n<td>Custom Business Logic / RPC on Object Structure</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Trigger Point</strong></td>\n<td>Message queues / Sync REST CRUD</td>\n<td><code>GET /oslc/os/<osname>?savedQuery=<name></code></td>\n<td><code>POST /oslc/os/<osname>/{id}?action=<name></code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Execution Model</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Callback Library (<code>INTERFACE = 1</code>)</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Procedural (<code>INTERFACE = 0</code>)</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Procedural (<code>INTERFACE = 0</code>)</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Backend Handler</strong></td>\n<td><code>MosProcessImpl</code> / <code>MosDefinitionImpl</code></td>\n<td><code>SavedQueryHandler.java</code></td>\n<td><code>ScriptActionHandler.java</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Auto-Save / Commit</strong></td>\n<td>Transaction pipeline commit</td>\n<td>Read-Only (No save)</td>\n<td>Automatically saves MboSet on successful POST/PATCH</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h3>Q5: What is the fundamental difference between External Exit and User Exit?</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>External Exit (<code>ScriptExternalExit.java</code>)</strong>:</li>\n<li><strong>Boundary</strong>: Outer network boundary between Maximo and external systems.</li>\n<li><strong>Problem Solved</strong>: Adapting non-standard external XML/JSON formats, cryptographic signatures, custom wrappers, and protocol headers.</li>\n<li><strong>Data Scope</strong>: Operates primarily on <strong><code>erData</code></strong> (External Record Data).</li>\n<li><strong>User Exit (<code>ScriptUserExit.java</code>)</strong>:</li>\n<li><strong>Boundary</strong>: Internal application domain between Channel Rules and Object Structures.</li>\n<li><strong>Problem Solved</strong>: Enforcing Maximo business rules, cross-field validations, database lookups, and conditional transaction drops (<code>service.raiseSkipTransaction()</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Data Scope</strong>: Operates on <strong><code>irData</code></strong> (Internal Record Data) and <code>erData</code>.</li>\n<p></ul>\n<h3>Q6: Why is there no Launch Point for End Point scripts in Automation Scripts?</h3></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Architectural Reason</strong>: Launch Points represent <strong>Event Triggers</strong>. An End Point is a <strong>Transport / Router Handler</strong> (<code>psdi.iface.router.*</code>), not an event listener.</li>\n<li><strong>How to Create</strong>:</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li>Create a <strong>Standalone Script (Script WITHOUT Launch Point)</strong> in Automation Scripts app (e.g. <code>SEND_TO_REST_API</code>).</li>\n<li>Create an End Point in <strong>End Points</strong> app with <strong>Handler = <code>SCRIPT</code></strong>.</li>\n<li>In the End Point Properties table, set property <strong><code>SCRIPT</code> = <code>SEND_TO_REST_API</code></strong>.</li>\n<li>ScriptRouterHandler.java automatically executes this script upon message routing.</li>\n</ol>\n</section>",
    "title_hi": "7.12: Frequently Asked Questions & Deep Technical Doubts (FAQs / Doubts)",
    "subtitle_hi": "INTERFACE = 1 vs 0 ka internal logic, hook lookup rules, aur interview questions.",
    "html_hi": "<h1>7.12: Frequently Asked Questions & Deep Technical Doubts (FAQs / Doubts)</h1>\n<p class=\"page-subtitle\">INTERFACE = 1 vs 0 ka internal logic, hook lookup rules, aur interview questions.</p>\n<section>\n<h3>Q1: <code>INTERFACE = 1</code> se kya lena dena hai? Ye execution ko kaise affect karta hai?</h3>\n<p><strong>Answer:</strong>\n<code>AUTOSCRIPT</code> database table me <code>INTERFACE</code> column ek boolean flag (<code>1</code> ya <code>0</code>) hota hai jo Maximo ke Scripting Engine ko yeh batata hai ki script ko <strong>kaise execute karna hai</strong>:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>INTERFACE = 0</code> (Normal Object / Attribute / Action Script):</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Maximo script ko ek single unit manta hai.</li>\n<li>Jab bhi trigger point fire hota hai, JSR223ScriptDriver.java poori script ko <strong>Line 1 se lekar end tak</strong> top-to-bottom sequentially execute (<code>cs.eval(sc)</code>) kar deta hai.</li>\n<p></ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>INTERFACE = 1</code> (Integration Script / Function Library):</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Maximo ko pata chal jata hai ki yeh ek <strong>Function Library / Callback Interface</strong> script hai.</li>\n<li>ScriptCacheImpl.java is script ko load karke functions ko compile karta hai aur JSR223ScriptDriver.java ise <code>invocableScriptCache</code> me rakh leta hai.</li>\n<li>Ab Maximo poori script ek saath nahi chalata, balki <strong>sirf required lifecycle function ko on-demand call karta hai</strong> via <code>((Invocable)engine).invokeFunction(functionName, args)</code>.</li></p>\n<p></ul>\n<blockquote class=\"ibm-blockquote\"><p><strong>Java Code Reference (JSR223ScriptDriver.java Line 245-266):</strong></p></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"ibm-blockquote\"><p>``<code>java</p></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"ibm-blockquote\"><p>if (scriptInfo.isInterfaceScript()) {</p></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"ibm-blockquote\"><p>ScriptEngine engine = (ScriptEngine)((Map)this.invocableScriptCache.get()).get(scriptInfo.getName());</p></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"ibm-blockquote\"><p>String functionName = (String)context.get(\"invokeFunction\");</p></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"ibm-blockquote\"><p>Object scrFunction = engine.get(functionName);</p></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"ibm-blockquote\"><p>if (scrFunction == null) {</p></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"ibm-blockquote\"><p>context.put(\"invokeStatus\", Boolean.valueOf(false));</p></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"ibm-blockquote\"><p>return;</p></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"ibm-blockquote\"><p>}</p></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"ibm-blockquote\"><p>context.put(\"invokeStatus\", Boolean.valueOf(true));</p></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"ibm-blockquote\"><p>Object[] args = (Object[])context.get(\"invokeArgs\");</p></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"ibm-blockquote\"><p>Object response = ((Invocable)engine).invokeFunction(functionName, args);</p></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"ibm-blockquote\"><p>context.put(\"invokeResponse\", response);</p></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"ibm-blockquote\"><p>}</p></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"ibm-blockquote\"><p></code>`<code></p></blockquote></p>\n<h3>Q2: </code>Invocable<code> ko kaise pata chalega maine kaunsa function script me likha hai? Kya missing functions par OOB (Out-Of-The-Box) logic chalega?</h3>\n<p><strong>Answer:</strong>\n<strong>Haan! Aapko saare 8 functions likhne ki zaroorat bilkul nahi hai.</strong></p>\n<p>Aap sirf wahi function likhte hain jahan custom requirement ho (jaise sirf </code>beforeMboData<code>), aur baaki sabhi lifecycle points par Maximo apna <strong>default OOB logic</strong> execute karta hai.</p>\n<h4>Backend Java Me Ye Kaise Handle Hota Hai?</h4>\nJab Maximo kisi hook par aata hai (e.g. </code>mboRules<code> ya </code>beforeProcess<code>), toh execution flow yeh hota hai:\n<ol>\n<li>Maximo script engine se poochta hai: </code>Object scrFunction = engine.get(functionName);<code></li>\n<li><strong>Agar aapne script me function NAHI likha hai:</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li></code>scrFunction == null<code> ho jata hai.</li>\n<li>Engine turant </code>invokeStatus = false<code> set karke return kar deta hai (koi crash ya </code>NoSuchMethodException<code> nahi aati).</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>MosProcessImpl.java Line 440 check karta hai:</strong></li>\n</ol>\n   </code>`<code>java\n   if (!hasInvokedScript(context)) {\n       return -1; // Fallback to standard OOB Maximo processing!\n   }\n   </code>`<code>\n   Iska matlab: Custom function nahi mila, toh Maximo bina ruke apna <strong>default Out-Of-The-Box logic</strong> chala deta hai!\n<h3>Q3: Kya naming pattern (</code>OSIN.<OSNAME><code>) exact hona zaroori hai ya kuch bhi naam de sakte hain?</h3>\n<p><strong>Answer:</strong>\n<strong>Haan! Object Structure aur Channel Exits ke liye naming pattern 100% STRICT aur MANDATORY hota hai.</strong> Aap koi arbitrary naam (jaise </code>MY_CUSTOM_SCRIPT<code>) nahi de sakte.</p>\n<h4>Kyun Zaroori Hai? (Java Code Lookup Mechanism):</h4>\nObject Structure application me script select karne ka koi dropdown ya field nahi hota. Maximo backend Java code script ko <strong>direct naming pattern</strong> se lookup karta hai:\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Inbound Engine (MosProcess.java Line 190):</strong></li>\n</ol>\n   Jab </code>MXWO<code> Object Structure me message aata hai, Java code internally yeh key create karta hai:\n   </code>`<code>java\n   this.scriptName = \"OSIN.\" + mosName; // Hardcoded string: \"OSIN.MXWO\"\n   </code>`<code>\n   Iske baad engine cache me check karta hai: </code>ScriptCache.getInstance().getScriptInfo(\"OSIN.MXWO\")<code>.\n<ul>\n<li>Agar naam </code>OSIN.MXWO<code> hai $\\rightarrow$ Script execute hogi.</li>\n<li>Agar aapne naam </code>CUSTOM_MXWO<code> rakh diya $\\rightarrow$ Maximo ko cache me </code>OSIN.MXWO<code> nahi milega, aur integration bina script ke normal chal jayegi.</li>\n<p></ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Outbound Engine (MosDefinitionImpl.java Line 186):</strong></li>\n</ol>\n   </code>`<code>java\n   this.scriptName = \"OSOUT.\" + mosName; // Hardcoded lookup: \"OSOUT.MXWO\"\n   </code>`<code></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Automation Scripts Application Ka Auto-Generation (AutoScript.java Line 938-1017):</strong></li>\n</ol>\n   Jab aap UI me <strong>\"Script for Integration\"</strong> chunte hain aur Object Structure </code>MXWO<code> select karte hain, toh Maximo backend MBO <strong>automatically script name field me </code>OSIN.MXWO<code> ya </code>OSOUT.MXWO<code> generate karke fill kar deta hai</strong> taaki user se typing mistake na ho!\n<h3>Q4: </code>OSQUERY<code> aur </code>OSACTION<code> me kya antar hai, aur ye </code>OSIN<code>/</code>OSOUT<code> se kaise alag hain?</h3>\n<p><strong>Answer:</strong></p>\n<p></code>OSIN<code> aur </code>OSOUT<code> jahan <strong>Data Sync & Inbound/Outbound Transformation</strong> ke liye use hote hain, wahin </code>OSQUERY<code> aur </code>OSACTION<code> Maximo ke <strong>Next-Gen REST/JSON & OSLC APIs</strong> ke liye banaye gaye specialized launch points hain:</p>\n<h4>Summary Comparison Table:</h4>\n<table class=\"ibm-data-table\">\n<thead><tr>\n<th>Parameter</th>\n<th></code>OSIN<code> / </code>OSOUT<code></th>\n<th></code>OSQUERY<code></th>\n<th></code>OSACTION<code></th>\n</tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Primary Goal</strong></td>\n<td>Inbound/Outbound Message Processing</td>\n<td>Dynamic REST API Filtering / Saved Queries</td>\n<td>Custom Business Logic / RPC on Object Structure</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Trigger Point</strong></td>\n<td>Message queue / Sync REST CRUD (POST, PUT)</td>\n<td><code>GET /oslc/os/<osname>?savedQuery=<name></code></td>\n<td><code>POST /oslc/os/<osname>/{id}?action=<name></code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Execution Style</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Interface Callback (<code>INTERFACE = 1</code>)</strong>: Specific lifecycle methods like <code>beforeMboData(ctx)</code> call hote hain.</td>\n<td><strong>Procedural Script (<code>INTERFACE = 0</code>)</strong>: Poori script top-to-bottom chalegi.</td>\n<td><strong>Procedural Script (<code>INTERFACE = 0</code>)</strong>: Poori script top-to-bottom chalegi.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Backend Java Handler</strong></td>\n<td><code>MosProcessImpl.java</code> / <code>MosDefinitionImpl.java</code></td>\n<td>SavedQueryHandler.java</td>\n<td>ScriptActionHandler.java</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Naming Pattern</strong></td>\n<td><code>OSIN.<OSNAME></code>, <code>OSOUT.<OSNAME></code></td>\n<td><code>OSQUERY.<OSNAME>.<QUERYNAME></code></td>\n<td><code>OSACTION.<OSNAME>.<ACTIONNAME></code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Key Variables</strong></td>\n<td><code>ctx</code> (<code>OSProcessScriptContext</code> / <code>OSDefnScriptContext</code>)</td>\n<td><code>mboset</code>, URL Query Parameters</td>\n<td><code>mbo</code>, <code>mboset</code>, <code>requestBody</code>, <code>responseBody</code>, <code>request</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Auto-Save / Commit</strong></td>\n<td>Maximo Transaction pipeline me save hota hai.</td>\n<td>Read-only (Query). Save nahi hota.</td>\n<td><code>ScriptActionHandler</code> script successful hone par automatically <code>mbo.getThisMboSet().save()</code> karta hai (POST/PATCH par).</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h4>Core Flow Samjhein:</h4>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Jab Dynamic Query chahiye</strong>: UI me <em>Object Structures $\\rightarrow$ OSLC Queries</em> me query banayein aur </code>OSQUERY.<OS>.<QUERY><code> script se URL parameters read karke </code>mboset.setWhere(...)<code> laga dein.</li>\n<li><strong>Jab Custom API Action chahiye</strong>: UI me <em>Object Structures $\\rightarrow$ OSLC Actions</em> me action banayein aur </code>OSACTION.<OS>.<ACTION><code> script se incoming </code>requestBody<code> parse karke MBO operations karein aur custom </code>responseBody<code> JSON return karein!</li>\n<p></ol>\n<h3>Q5: External Exit aur User Exit me main antar kya hai aur kab kaunsa use karein?</h3></p>\n<p><strong>Answer:</strong></p>\n<p>Dono me sabse bada antar unka <strong>Architecture Level Boundary</strong> aur <strong>Data Scope</strong> hai:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>External Exit (</code>ScriptExternalExit.java<code>)</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Boundary</strong>: Yeh Maximo ke <strong>sabse bahar (Network / External Boundary)</strong> baithta hai.</li>\n<li><strong>Kab use karein</strong>: Jab external system ka format standard na ho (e.g. non-standard XML/JSON envelopes, base64 payload encryption/decryption, vendor-specific security headers, external date string conversions).</li>\n<li><strong>Data Format</strong>: Yeh primarily <strong></code>erData<code> (External Record Data)</strong> par kaam karta hai.</li>\n<li><strong>Timing</strong>:</li>\n<li><em>Inbound</em>: Sabse pehle chalta hai (</code>EXTEXIT.IN<code>), Processing Rules se bhi pehle.</li>\n<li><em>Outbound</em>: Sabse aakhiri me chalta hai (</code>EXTEXIT.OUT<code>), End Point dispatch se theek pehle.</li>\n<p></ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>User Exit (</code>ScriptUserExit.java<code>)</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Boundary</strong>: Yeh Maximo ke <strong>business application domain</strong> ke andar baithta hai (Channel Rules aur Object Structure ke beech).</li>\n<li><strong>Kab use karein</strong>: Jab Maximo business rules apply karne hon (e.g. kisi condition par transaction silently drop karna via </code>service.raiseSkipTransaction()<code>, Maximo database se additional related MBOs lookup karke internal field bharna).</li>\n<li><strong>Data Format</strong>: Yeh <strong></code>irData<code> (Internal Record Data)</strong> aur </code>erData<code> dono par operate karta hai.</li>\n<li><strong>Timing</strong>:</li>\n<li><em>Inbound</em>: </code>USEREXIT.IN.BEFORE<code> (erData), </code>USEREXIT.IN.AFTER<code> (irData + erData), </code>USEREXIT.IN.MBO<code> (MBO level).</li>\n<li><em>Outbound</em>: </code>USEREXIT.OUT.BEFORE<code> (irData), </code>USEREXIT.OUT.AFTER<code> (irData + erData).</li></p>\n<p></ul>\n<h3>Q6: Automation Scripts App me End Point ke liye Launch Point kyun nahi mil raha? Script kaise banegi?</h3></p>\n<p><strong>Answer:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Automation Scripts me End Point ka koi Launch Point hota hi nahi hai!</strong></p>\n<h4>Iski Wajah:</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Maximo me Launch Points <strong>Event Triggers</strong> (jaise Object Save, Attribute Validate, Action Run, Object Structure Process) ke liye hote hain.</li>\n<li>End Point koi event nahi hai; yeh ek <strong>Router / Transport Handler</strong> (</code>psdi.iface.router.<em><code>) hai (jaise </code>HTTP<code>, </code>JMS<code>, </code>FLATFILE<code>, </code>WEBSERVICE<code>).</li>\n<li>Maximo ne router layer par ek generic handler banaya hai jiska naam hai <strong></code>SCRIPT<code></strong> (ScriptRouterHandler.java).</li>\n<p></ul>\n<h4>Real Configuration Flow:</h4>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Automation Scripts App</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Click <strong>Create</strong> $\\rightarrow$ <strong>Script</strong> (</em>Script WITHOUT Launch Point / Standalone Script*).</li>\n<li>Name: e.g. </code>SEND_TO_REST_API<code>.</li>\n<li>Script me </code>requestDataS<code> se payload read karein aur </code>service.httppostasjson(...)<code> call karke </code>responseData<code> set karein.</li>\n<li>Status: <strong>ACTIVE</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>End Points App (</code>Integration -> End Points<code>)</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Create New End Point (e.g. </code>MY_REST_EP<code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Handler</strong> dropdown me select karein: <strong></code>SCRIPT<code></strong>.</li>\n<li>Niche Properties table me <strong></code>SCRIPT<code></strong> property ki value set karein: </code>SEND_TO_REST_API<code>.</li>\n<li>Optional properties jaise </code>URL<code>, </code>AUTH_TOKEN<code>, </code>TIMEOUT<code> bhi properties table me add kar sakte hain.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Attach End Point</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Apne Publish Channel ya External System me jaakar </code>End Point = MY_REST_EP<code> select kar dein.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Execution Mechanics</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Jab message router par aata hai, ScriptRouterHandler.java End Point properties se </code>SCRIPT<code> property ka naam read karta hai, </code>requestData<code> aur </code>requestDataS<code> inject karta hai, aur script execute karke </code>responseData` return karta hai!</li>\n</ul></p>\n</section>"
  }
};
